{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T16:46:15.606433", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Return a sequence of actions that makes a stick in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  This implementation delegates the planning to the helper function\n  ``craft.make`` which knows how to:\n    1. Retrieve the recipe for the requested item,\n    2. Locate the required primitive resources in the world,\n    3. Move the agent to collect them,\n    4. Bring the resources to the appropriate workshop and perform the craft.\n\n  Args:\n      env: An instance of the CraftWorld environment.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially\n      in the environment, will result in the agent possessing at least one\n      ``stick`` item.\n  \"\"\"\n  # The ``craft`` module provides a generic planner for any goal item.\n  # By passing the goal name ``'stick'`` we obtain the full action plan.\n  return craft.make(env, \"stick\")", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
