{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T16:50:41.904614", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Return a list of movement actions (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that moves\n  from ``start`` to ``goal`` using a simple Manhattan\u2011grid strategy.\n  \"\"\"\n  y, x = start\n  gy, gx = goal\n  actions = []\n\n  # vertical moves\n  while y < gy:\n      actions.append(DOWN)\n      y += 1\n  while y > gy:\n      actions.append(UP)\n      y -= 1\n\n  # horizontal moves\n  while x < gx:\n      actions.append(RIGHT)\n      x += 1\n  while x > gx:\n      actions.append(LEFT)\n      x -= 1\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T16:50:43.015907", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that will result in a stick being\n  present in the agent's inventory.\n\n  The function works with any `CraftWorld` environment that follows the\n  standard API used throughout the repository:\n\n  * ``env.cookbook`` \u2013 a :class:`Cookbook` instance exposing the recipe\n    information.\n  * ``env.world`` \u2013 the underlying :class:`CraftWorld` object.\n  * ``env.step(action)`` \u2013 apply an action and advance the simulation.\n  * ``env.pos`` \u2013 the current (x, y) position of the agent.\n  * ``env.dir`` \u2013 the current facing direction (0\u20113).\n  * ``env.grid`` \u2013 the current grid representation.\n  * ``env.inventory`` \u2013 a ``np.ndarray`` with the current inventory counts.\n\n  The implementation follows three simple steps:\n\n  1. Retrieve the recipe for ``stick`` from the ``Cookbook``.  The recipe\n     maps primitive kind indices to the required count.\n  2. For every required primitive, repeatedly move the agent to a cell\n     that contains that primitive and execute the ``USE`` action until\n     the needed amount has been collected.\n  3. Once all primitives are in the inventory, move the agent to a\n     workshop that can craft a stick and issue a ``USE`` action to perform\n     the crafting.\n\n  The helper ``_move_to`` performs a Manhattan\u2011distance greedy walk\n  towards a target cell while avoiding blocked cells.  The helper\n  ``_find_nearest`` scans the grid for the closest cell that contains a\n  given kind index.\n\n  The function returns the list of actions (integers) that were sent to\n  the environment.\n  \"\"\"\n  # action constants \u2013 they are defined in the original repository;\n  # we fall back to the conventional ordering if they are missing.\n  DOWN = getattr(env, \"DOWN\", 0)\n  UP = getattr(env, \"UP\", 1)\n  LEFT = getattr(env, \"LEFT\", 2)\n  RIGHT = getattr(env, \"RIGHT\", 3)\n  USE = getattr(env, \"USE\", 4)\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1.  Look up the recipe for ``stick``.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  stick_idx = env.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  recipe = env.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  # ``recipe`` is a mapping {primitive_idx: count, \"_at\": workshop_idx}\n  primitive_reqs = {k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if k != \"_at\"}\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2.  Helper functions for navigation.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def _move_to(target):\n      \"\"\"Greedy Manhattan walk from the current position to *target*.\"\"\"\n      while env.pos != target:\n          x, y = env.pos\n          tx, ty = target\n          if x < tx:\n              act = RIGHT\n              env.step(act)\n              actions.append(act)\n          elif x > tx:\n              act = LEFT\n              env.step(act)\n              actions.append(act)\n          elif y < ty:\n              act = DOWN\n              env.step(act)\n              actions.append(act)\n          elif y > ty:\n              act = UP\n              env.step(act)\n              actions.append(act)\n\n  def _find_nearest(kind_idx):\n      \"\"\"Return the coordinates of the closest cell that contains *kind_idx*.\"\"\"\n      grid = env.grid\n      h, w, _ = grid.shape\n      best = None\n      best_dist = None\n      for iy in range(h):\n          for ix in range(w):\n              if grid[iy, ix, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  dist = abs(ix - env.pos[0]) + abs(iy - env.pos[1])\n                  if best is None or dist < best_dist:\n                      best = (ix, iy)\n                      best_dist = dist\n      return best\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3.  Collect all required primitives.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_reqs.items():\n      while env.inventory[prim_idx] < needed:\n          target = _find_nearest(prim_idx)\n          if target is None:\n              # No reachable primitive \u2013 abort early.\n              return actions\n          _move_to(target)\n          # The agent is now standing on a cell that contains the primitive.\n          # Use the cell to pick it up.\n          env.step(USE)\n          actions.append(USE)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4.  Craft the stick at the appropriate workshop (if any).\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      workshop_cell = _find_nearest(workshop_idx)\n      if workshop_cell is not None:\n          _move_to(workshop_cell)\n          env.step(USE)\n          actions.append(USE)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
