{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T16:57:56.304810", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  The function:\n    1. Looks up the recipe for ``stick`` in the world's cookbook.\n    2. Finds the required primitive resources on the current grid.\n    3. Moves the agent to each primitive, uses the ``USE`` action to pick it up,\n       and finally moves to the required workshop (if any) and uses ``USE`` to\n       craft the stick.\n\n  The returned list contains action indices compatible with the environment's\n  action space:\n\n      0 \u2013 DOWN\n      1 \u2013 UP\n      2 \u2013 LEFT\n      3 \u2013 RIGHT\n      4 \u2013 USE\n\n  The implementation is deliberately simple: it assumes the grid is free of\n  obstacles that would block a Manhattan\u2011style path.  If a needed primitive or\n  workshop cannot be found, the function simply skips that step.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instantiated CraftLab / CraftWorld environment.  It must expose the\n      attributes ``_current_state`` (a ``CraftState``) and ``world`` (a\n      ``CraftWorld``).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially, should\n      result in the agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Helper constants \u2013 match the environment's action specifications.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Grab the current state and world objects.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  state = env._current_state          # type: CraftState\n  world = env.world                    # type: CraftWorld\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Identify the index for the target item (``stick``) and fetch its recipe.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n\n  # Separate primitive requirements from the workshop specification.\n  primitives_needed = {k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if k != \"_at\"}\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n\n  actions = []          # final action list to be returned\n  pos = state.pos       # current (x, y) position of the agent\n  grid = state.grid     # (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds) occupancy tensor\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Utility: locate any cell that contains a given kind (primitive or workshop).\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  def locate_kind(kind):\n      \"\"\"Return the (x, y) coordinate of the first cell containing ``kind``.\"\"\"\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind] > 0)\n      if locations.size == 0:\n          return None\n      # ``np.argwhere`` returns rows as (x, y); keep the first match.\n      return tuple(locations[0].tolist())\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Utility: generate a Manhattan path from the current position to ``target``.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  def move_to(target):\n      \"\"\"Append actions that move the agent from ``pos`` to ``target``.\"\"\"\n      nonlocal pos, actions\n      if target is None:\n          return\n      tx, ty = target\n      x, y = pos\n\n      # Move horizontally (x\u2011axis) first.\n      while x < tx:\n          actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n          x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          actions.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n          x -= 1\n\n      # Then move vertically (y\u2011axis).\n      while y < ty:\n          actions.append(ACTION_DOWN)\n          y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          actions.append(ACTION_UP)\n          y -= 1\n\n      pos = (x, y)\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Collect all required primitives according to the recipe.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  for kind, count in primitives_needed.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          loc = locate_kind(kind)\n          if loc is None:\n              # Primitive not found \u2013 skip this instance.\n              continue\n          move_to(loc)\n          actions.append(ACTION_USE)   # pick up the primitive\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Finally, go to the workshop (if the recipe specifies one) and craft.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      workshop_loc = locate_kind(workshop_idx)\n      if workshop_loc is not None:\n          move_to(workshop_loc)\n          actions.append(ACTION_USE)   # craft the stick\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
