{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:08:38.003439", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that will collect the required primitives\n  for a ``stick`` and then craft the stick at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  The implementation works with any CraftWorld / CraftLab environment\n  that follows the API described in the prompt.  It does **not** execute\n  the actions \u2013 it only returns the sequence of action indices that\n  should be fed to ``env.step`` later.\n\n  The algorithm is deliberately simple:\n    1.  Identify the index of the goal item (``stick``) and the\n        primitives required to craft one stick.\n    2.  Repeatedly locate each needed primitive on the grid,\n        move the agent to that cell and issue a ``USE`` action to pick it\n        up.\n    3.  Locate the workshop required for the ``stick`` recipe,\n        move to it and ``USE`` to craft the item.\n\n  The movement strategy is a Manhattan walk (first vertical then\n  horizontal).  It assumes the environment does not contain dynamic\n  obstacles that would block this na\u00efve path \u2013 which is a safe\n  assumption for the static CraftWorld scenarios used in the tests.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      A CraftLab (or compatible) environment instance.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action integers that, when executed in order, will\n      produce a ``stick`` in the agent's inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def _manhattan_actions(start, goal, act_map):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of actions that walk from start to goal using a\n      simple Manhattan strategy (vertical then horizontal).\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      y, x = start\n      gy, gx = goal\n\n      # vertical moves\n      while y < gy:\n          actions.append(act_map[\"DOWN\"])\n          y += 1\n      while y > gy:\n          actions.append(act_map[\"UP\"])\n          y -= 1\n      # horizontal moves\n      while x < gx:\n          actions.append(act_map[\"RIGHT\"])\n          x += 1\n      while x > gx:\n          actions.append(act_map[\"LEFT\"])\n          x -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Initialise \u2013 obtain the current state without stepping the env.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Reset (or assume already reset) to obtain a fresh observation.\n  # The CraftLab stores the live state in a protected attribute.\n  _ = env.reset()\n  state = env._current_state      # type: CraftState\n\n  # Action mapping (e.g. {\"DOWN\":0, \"UP\":1, ...})\n  act_map = env.action_specs()\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Identify the goal (stick) and its recipe.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]          # integer id of the goal\n  # Primitive requirements for ONE stick (may include intermediate items)\n  needed = cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)  # dict {kind_idx: count}\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Simulated mutable copies of the world state (so we can plan without\n  # actually stepping the environment).\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  grid = state.grid.copy()                     # (W, H, n_kinds)\n  inv = state.inventory.copy()                 # (n_kinds,)\n  pos = tuple(state.pos)                       # (y, x)\n\n  actions_plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Collect each required primitive.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for kind, required_cnt in needed.items():\n      while inv[kind] < required_cnt:\n          # Locate any cell that still contains the primitive.\n          locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              raise RuntimeError(\n                  f\"Cannot find required primitive (kind={kind}) on the grid.\"\n              )\n          ty, tx = locations[0]  # pick the first occurrence\n\n          # Move to that cell.\n          actions_plan.extend(_manhattan_actions(pos, (ty, tx), act_map))\n          pos = (ty, tx)  # update simulated position\n\n          # Pick it up.\n          actions_plan.append(act_map[\"USE\"])\n\n          # Update simulated world: remove from grid, add to inventory.\n          grid[ty, tx, kind] -= 1\n          inv[kind] += 1\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Craft the stick at its designated workshop.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx]\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]               # e.g. \"workbench\"\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # Find a workshop cell (any will do).\n  workshop_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n  if workshop_cells.size == 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(\"No workshop cell for stick found on the grid.\")\n  wy, wx = workshop_cells[0]\n\n  # Move to the workshop cell.\n  actions_plan.extend(_manhattan_actions(pos, (wy, wx), act_map))\n  pos = (wy, wx)\n\n  # Use the workshop to craft the stick.\n  actions_plan.append(act_map[\"USE\"])\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Return the complete action list.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  return actions_plan", "env_interactions": 4, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:08:39.145970", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a list of actions that makes a stick in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.  The implementation extracts the recipe for the item\n  ``stick`` from the world\u2019s cookbook, collects the required primitive\n  resources, and finally crafts the stick at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  The returned list can be fed directly to ``env.step(action)`` in order.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Mapping of movement actions \u2013 they are defined in the ``env`` module.\n  # If they are not present we fall back to the usual integer encoding.\n  DOWN = getattr(env, \"DOWN\", 0)\n  UP = getattr(env, \"UP\", 1)\n  LEFT = getattr(env, \"LEFT\", 2)\n  RIGHT = getattr(env, \"RIGHT\", 3)\n  USE = getattr(env, \"USE\", 4)\n\n  # Simple Manhattan\u2011style path planner.\n  def plan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of movement actions to go from start to goal.\"\"\"\n      x, y = start\n      gx, gy = goal\n      actions = []\n      # move in x direction\n      while x < gx:\n          actions.append(RIGHT); x += 1\n      while x > gx:\n          actions.append(LEFT);  x -= 1\n      # move in y direction\n      while y < gy:\n          actions.append(DOWN);  y += 1\n      while y > gy:\n          actions.append(UP);    y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # Find a free neighbour (4\u2011connected) of a given cell.\n  def free_neighbour(cell, grid):\n      \"\"\"Return a coordinate adjacent to *cell* that is empty.\"\"\"\n      w, h, _ = grid.shape\n      cx, cy = cell\n      for dx, dy in [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]:\n          nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n          if 0 <= nx < w and 0 <= ny < h:\n              # a cell is free when the sum over all kinds is zero\n              if not grid[nx, ny].any():\n                  return (nx, ny)\n      # fallback \u2013 if no free neighbour (should not happen in normal maps)\n      return cell\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Extract world information\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world if hasattr(env, \"world\") else env._current_state.world\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  # Index of the target item (stick)\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # Full recipe dict for the stick (includes ingredients and workshop)\n  stick_recipe = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Determine which primitives are required (ignore the special \"_at\" key)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  primitive_needs = {\n      kind: cnt\n      for kind, cnt in stick_recipe.items()\n      if kind != \"_at\"\n  }\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Starting position (the agent\u2019s current location)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  state = env._current_state\n  pos = tuple(state.pos)          # (x, y)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Build the action list\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Collect each required primitive.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  grid = state.grid.copy()        # current occupancy\n  for prim_kind, needed in primitive_needs.items():\n      # locate all cells that contain this primitive\n      prim_cells = list(zip(*np.where(grid[:, :, prim_kind] > 0)))\n      # we may need multiple copies \u2013 take the first *needed* cells\n      for i in range(needed):\n          if not prim_cells:\n              raise RuntimeError(\"Required primitive not found in the map\")\n          target = prim_cells.pop(0)               # (x, y) of the primitive\n          # Move to a free neighbour of the primitive\n          neigh = free_neighbour(target, grid)\n          actions.extend(plan_path(pos, neigh))\n          pos = neigh                               # update simulated position\n          # Face the primitive (the direction after the last move already\n          # points toward the neighbour; we just need to USE)\n          actions.append(USE)\n          # Update the simulated grid: the primitive is now in the inventory\n          grid[target[0], target[1], prim_kind] -= 1\n          # (the inventory is handled by the environment when actions are\n          # actually executed, so we only keep the grid consistent here)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Move to the required workshop and craft the stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  workshop_kind = stick_recipe[\"_at\"]\n  # locate a workshop of the required type\n  workshop_cells = list(zip(*np.where(grid[:, :, workshop_kind] > 0)))\n  if not workshop_cells:\n      raise RuntimeError(\"No workshop of the required type found\")\n  workshop = workshop_cells[0]\n  # Move next to the workshop\n  neigh = free_neighbour(workshop, grid)\n  actions.extend(plan_path(pos, neigh))\n  pos = neigh\n  # Use the workshop to craft the stick\n  actions.append(USE)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Return the complete action list\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
