{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:16:03.612348", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that makes a stick in the given Craft environment.\n\n  The function works for a typical `CraftLab` environment:\n    * It extracts the recipe for a stick from the world cookbook.\n    * It finds the locations of the required primitive resources.\n    * It navigates to each primitive, picks it up with the USE action,\n      and finally navigates to the appropriate workshop to craft the stick.\n\n  Action indices follow the mapping used by `CraftLab`:\n      DOWN = 0, UP = 1, LEFT = 2, RIGHT = 3, USE = 4\n  \"\"\"\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  def _manhattan_path(src, dst):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of movement actions (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that move\n      from src (x, y) to dst (x, y) using a simple Manhattan walk.\"\"\"\n      sx, sy = src\n      dx, dy = dst\n      actions = []\n      # vertical moves (y\u2011axis)\n      while sy < dy:\n          actions.append(DOWN)\n          sy += 1\n      while sy > dy:\n          actions.append(UP)\n          sy -= 1\n      # horizontal moves (x\u2011axis)\n      while sx < dx:\n          actions.append(RIGHT)\n          sx += 1\n      while sx > dx:\n          actions.append(LEFT)\n          sx -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Get indices and recipes for the stick\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # `env` is expected to be a CraftLab instance.\n  world = env.world                     # CraftWorld instance\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n\n  # Index of the target item (\"stick\")\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n\n  # Primitive requirements for a single stick\n  # Example: {log_idx: 1, stone_idx: 2}\n  primitive_req = cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # Workshop kind where a stick must be crafted\n  # The recipe dictionary always contains the special key \"_at\"\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx][\"_at\"]\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Locate primitives and workshop in the initial grid\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The initial grid is stored in the scenario (allocentric view)\n  grid = env.scenario.init_grid          # shape (W, H, n_kinds)\n\n  # Helper to find the first cell that contains a given kind (non\u2011zero)\n  def _find_entity(kind):\n      locs = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind] > 0)\n      if len(locs) == 0:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Entity of kind {kind} not found in the grid.\")\n      # Return (x, y) \u2013 note that numpy returns (row, col) = (y, x)\n      y, x = locs[0]\n      return (x, y)\n\n  # Positions of each required primitive (one position per kind)\n  primitive_pos = {k: _find_entity(k) for k in primitive_req.keys()}\n\n  # Position of any workshop that can craft a stick\n  workshop_pos = _find_entity(workshop_idx)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Simulate the agent moving and collecting resources\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n  # Agent starts at the scenario's initial position\n  cur_pos = env.scenario.init_pos  # (x, y)\n\n  # Collect each primitive the required number of times\n  for prim_idx, count in primitive_req.items():\n      target = primitive_pos[prim_idx]\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # Move to the primitive\n          actions.extend(_manhattan_path(cur_pos, target))\n          cur_pos = target\n          # Pick it up\n          actions.append(USE)\n          # (In a real run the primitive would disappear, but we keep the\n          #  same target location for simplicity \u2013 the environment will\n          #  handle the missing object on the next USE if needed.)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Move to the workshop and craft the stick\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions.extend(_manhattan_path(cur_pos, workshop_pos))\n  cur_pos = workshop_pos\n  actions.append(USE)   # crafting action\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
