{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:22:45.486530", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given\n  :class:`CraftLab`/environment instance.\n\n  The function first checks whether the environment provides a high\u2011level\n  ``craft`` helper (as is the case for the reference implementation in the\n  repository).  If such a helper exists, it is used directly \u2013 it returns the\n  list of integer actions required to collect the necessary primitives and\n  perform the crafting operation at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  If the helper is not present, the function falls back to an empty list,\n  which is a safe no\u2011op (the caller can decide how to handle this case).\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the Craft environment (e.g. ``CraftLab`` or a raw\n      ``CraftWorld`` wrapper).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially in the\n      environment, will result in the agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Preferred path: use the high\u2011level crafting helper if it exists.\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      # ``env.craft`` is expected to accept the name of the desired item and\n      # return a ready\u2011to\u2011execute action list.\n      try:\n          return env.craft(\"stick\")\n      except Exception:\n          # If the helper raises (e.g. unknown item), fall back to safe default.\n          pass\n\n  # If no helper is available, we cannot construct a plan without deeper\n  # knowledge of the grid layout.  Returning an empty list is a safe no\u2011op.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:22:46.622898", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:23:00.609135", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"Generate a list of movement actions (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that\n  moves from start to goal using a simple Manhattan walk.\"\"\"\n  actions = []\n  x, y = start\n  gx, gy = goal\n\n  # vertical moves (y axis)\n  while y < gy:\n      actions.append(DOWN)\n      y += 1\n  while y > gy:\n      actions.append(UP)\n      y -= 1\n\n  # horizontal moves (x axis)\n  while x < gx:\n      actions.append(RIGHT)\n      x += 1\n  while x > gx:\n      actions.append(LEFT)\n      x -= 1\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:23:01.914888", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Simple placeholder implementation for the `make_stick` task.\n\n  Since the specifics of the environment's API and the recipe details are\n  not available in this context, the function returns an empty list of\n  actions, which satisfies the required return type (a list of action\n  indices).  This can be replaced with a proper planning routine that\n  queries the environment for primitive locations, moves the agent, and\n  performs the necessary craft actions.\n\n  Args:\n      env: The CraftWorld environment instance (unused in this stub).\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: An empty list of actions.\n  \"\"\"\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:23:26.846242", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of actions that will make a *stick* in the given\n  CraftLab environment.\n\n  The implementation follows a very simple planner:\n\n  1.  Look up the index of the item ``stick`` in the world cookbook.\n  2.  Query the recipe for ``stick`` to obtain the required primitive\n      kinds and their counts as well as the workshop where the item must\n      be crafted.\n  3.  For each required primitive:\n      *   Find the nearest cell that contains the primitive.\n      *   Move the agent to that cell (using Manhattan moves only).\n      *   Execute the ``USE`` action to pick it up.\n  4.  Move to the required workshop and execute ``USE`` once to craft\n      the stick.\n\n  The function does **not** try to be optimal \u2013 it merely produces a\n  correct sequence of actions for any environment that follows the\n  specification described in the prompt.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Action constants \u2013 they match the ordering used by CraftLab.\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  def manhattan(a, b):\n      \"\"\"Manhattan distance between two (x, y) tuples.\"\"\"\n      return abs(a[0] - b[0]) + abs(a[1] - b[1])\n\n  def move_towards(src, dst):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generate a list of movement actions that brings the agent from\n      ``src`` to ``dst`` using only horizontal and vertical steps.\n      The function prefers horizontal moves first, then vertical.\n      \"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      x, y = src\n      tx, ty = dst\n\n      # Horizontal moves\n      while x < tx:\n          actions.append(RIGHT)\n          x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          actions.append(LEFT)\n          x -= 1\n\n      # Vertical moves\n      while y < ty:\n          actions.append(DOWN)\n          y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          actions.append(UP)\n          y -= 1\n\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Access the underlying CraftState from the Lab wrapper.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  state = env._current_state          # type: CraftState\n  world = env.world                    # type: CraftWorld\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Find the index of the target item (\"stick\").\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Retrieve the recipe for the stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  # ``recipe`` is a dict where keys are ingredient indices (int) and\n  # values are required counts (int).  The workshop is stored under the\n  # special key \"_at\".\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  # Remove the workshop entry so that we are left only with primitive\n  # requirements.\n  primitive_requirements = {\n      k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if k != \"_at\"\n  }\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Collect all required primitives.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n  cur_pos = state.pos  # (x, y)\n\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_requirements.items():\n      # Find all cells that currently contain this primitive.\n      # ``grid`` has shape (W, H, n_kinds) and is one\u2011hot.\n      locations = list(zip(*np.where(state.grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)))\n      # If for some reason there are no locations (should not happen in\n      # a valid scenario) we simply skip.\n      if not locations:\n          continue\n\n      # Repeatedly collect the required number of that primitive.\n      for _ in range(needed):\n          # Choose the nearest location (Manhattan distance).\n          nearest = min(locations, key=lambda p: manhattan(cur_pos, p))\n\n          # Move to that location.\n          actions.extend(move_towards(cur_pos, nearest))\n          cur_pos = nearest\n\n          # Pick it up.\n          actions.append(USE)\n\n          # Update the internal view of the grid \u2013 after a successful\n          # ``USE`` the primitive disappears from the cell.\n          # (We do not modify the real environment here; the plan is\n          #  based on the assumption that the action will succeed.)\n          # Remove the used location from future consideration.\n          locations.remove(nearest)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Move to the workshop and craft the stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      # Locate all workshop cells of the required type.\n      workshop_cells = list(zip(*np.where(state.grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)))\n      if workshop_cells:\n          # Choose the nearest workshop.\n          target_ws = min(workshop_cells, key=lambda p: manhattan(cur_pos, p))\n          actions.extend(move_towards(cur_pos, target_ws))\n          cur_pos = target_ws\n          # Craft the stick.\n          actions.append(USE)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:23:27.986032", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that makes the agent craft a ``stick`` in the\n  given CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation is completely generic \u2013 it does **not** rely on any\n  hard\u2011coded map layout.  It works by:\n\n  1.  Querying the world\u2019s ``Cookbook`` for the index of the goal item\n      (``stick``) and the primitive ingredients required to craft it.\n  2.  Repeatedly locating the closest cell that contains a required primitive,\n      moving the agent there (using a shortest\u2011path BFS that respects blocked\n      cells) and executing the ``USE`` action to pick it up.\n  3.  After all ingredients have been collected, locating the appropriate\n      workshop (if the recipe specifies one) and using ``USE`` there to craft\n      the stick.\n  4.  Returning the full sequence of action indices.\n\n  The function assumes the standard action encoding used by the CraftWorld\n  implementation:\n\n      0 \u2013 DOWN\n      1 \u2013 UP\n      2 \u2013 LEFT\n      3 \u2013 RIGHT\n      4 \u2013 USE   (collect / craft)\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      A running CraftWorld / CraftLab environment.  The function expects the\n      environment to expose the following attributes (as defined in the\n      code base description):\n\n      * ``world`` \u2013 the ``CraftWorld`` instance.\n      * ``_current_state`` \u2013 the current ``CraftState``.\n      * ``task`` \u2013 a ``Task`` named\u2011tuple with a ``goal`` field that holds the\n        integer index of the desired item.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when fed to ``env.step(action)`` in order,\n      will result in the agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  import collections\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Helper functions\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  def bfs(start, target_kind):\n      \"\"\"\n      Bread\u2011first search for the nearest cell that contains ``target_kind``.\n      Returns a list of movement actions (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that bring the\n      agent from ``start`` to the target cell, or ``None`` if no reachable\n      cell exists.\n      \"\"\"\n      W, H, K = state.grid.shape\n      visited = np.full((W, H), False, dtype=bool)\n      q = collections.deque()\n      q.append((start, []))\n      visited[start] = True\n\n      # movement deltas and corresponding action indices\n      moves = [((0, 1), 0),   # DOWN\n               ((0, -1), 1),  # UP\n               ((-1, 0), 2),  # LEFT\n               ((1, 0), 3)]   # RIGHT\n\n      while q:\n          (x, y), path = q.popleft()\n          # if the current cell contains the target kind, we are done\n          if state.grid[x, y, target_kind] > 0:\n              return path\n\n          for (dx, dy), act in moves:\n              nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n              if 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H and not visited[nx, ny]:\n                  # a cell is *blocked* if any non\u2011zero entry exists for a\n                  # non\u2011grabbable kind (environment entities).  We treat a\n                  # cell as passable if it contains only empty (0) or\n                  # grabbable items.\n                  cell = state.grid[nx, ny]\n                  blocked = False\n                  for kind_idx, cnt in enumerate(cell):\n                      if cnt > 0 and kind_idx in world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                          blocked = True\n                          break\n                  if not blocked:\n                      visited[nx, ny] = True\n                      q.append(((nx, ny), path + [act]))\n      return None\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Main logic\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  world = env.world\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # 1. Identify the goal index for \u201cstick\u201d.\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # 2. Determine which primitives (and how many) are needed.\n  primitives_needed = world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Collect each required primitive.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  for prim_idx, count in primitives_needed.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # locate the nearest instance of this primitive\n          path = bfs(state.pos, prim_idx)\n          if path is None:\n              raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot reach primitive {prim_idx}\")\n\n          # execute movement actions\n          for act in path:\n              obs, reward, done, info = env.step(act)\n              actions.append(act)\n              state = env._current_state   # update reference after the step\n\n          # now we are on the cell containing the primitive \u2013 use it\n          obs, reward, done, info = env.step(4)   # USE\n          actions.append(4)\n          state = env._current_state\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Craft the stick at the required workshop (if any).\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n\n  if workshop_name is not None:\n      workshop_idx = world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n      path = bfs(state.pos, workshop_idx)\n      if path is None:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot reach workshop {workshop_name}\")\n\n      for act in path:\n          obs, reward, done, info = env.step(act)\n          actions.append(act)\n          state = env._current_state\n\n      # use the workshop to craft the stick\n      obs, reward, done, info = env.step(4)   # USE\n      actions.append(4)\n      state = env._current_state\n  else:\n      # No specific workshop \u2013 a simple USE on the current cell crafts.\n      obs, reward, done, info = env.step(4)\n      actions.append(4)\n      state = env._current_state\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
