{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:25:57.668820", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that will make a **stick** in the given\n  CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation works for any version of the environment that follows\n  the API described in the prompt:\n\n  * ``env.world`` is a :class:`CraftWorld` instance.\n  * ``env.world.cookbook`` provides the recipe information.\n  * ``env._current_state`` holds the current :class:`CraftState`.\n  * The action space is assumed to be:\n        0 \u2013 DOWN, 1 \u2013 UP, 2 \u2013 LEFT, 3 \u2013 RIGHT, 4 \u2013 USE\n\n  The algorithm is:\n\n  1.  Look up the index of the goal item (``stick``).\n  2.  Retrieve the primitive requirements for that goal via\n      ``cookbook.primitives_for``.\n  3.  For each required primitive (and the required count) find a cell\n      that contains it and plan a shortest path from the agent\u2019s current\n      position to that cell, avoiding non\u2011grabbable entities.\n  4.  Append the movement actions for the path and a ``USE`` action to\n      collect the primitive.\n  5.  After all primitives have been collected, move to the workshop\n      required for the final crafting step (the ``_at`` field of the\n      recipe) and issue a final ``USE`` to craft the stick.\n\n  The function returns a flat ``list[int]`` containing the actions.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  import collections\n\n  # Mapping from (dx, dy) to the action index expected by the environment.\n  # The mapping follows the convention used by the original CraftWorld:\n  #   0 \u2013 DOWN, 1 \u2013 UP, 2 \u2013 LEFT, 3 \u2013 RIGHT\n  DIR_TO_ACTION = {\n      (0, 1): 0,   # down  (y+1)\n      (0, -1): 1,  # up    (y-1)\n      (-1, 0): 2,  # left  (x-1)\n      (1, 0): 3,   # right (x+1)\n  }\n\n  def bfs(start, goal_cells, walkable):\n      \"\"\"Bread\u2011first search returning a list of positions from ``start`` to\n      the nearest cell in ``goal_cells`` (both given as (x, y) tuples).\n\n      ``walkable`` is a 2\u2011D boolean array where ``True`` indicates that the\n      agent can step on the cell.\n      \"\"\"\n      w, h = walkable.shape\n      q = collections.deque([start])\n      prev = {start: None}\n      while q:\n          cur = q.popleft()\n          if cur in goal_cells:\n              # reconstruct path\n              path = []\n              while cur != start:\n                  path.append(cur)\n                  cur = prev[cur]\n              path.reverse()\n              return path\n          x, y = cur\n          for dx, dy in DIR_TO_ACTION.keys():\n              nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n              if 0 <= nx < w and 0 <= ny < h and walkable[nx, ny]:\n                  nxt = (nx, ny)\n                  if nxt not in prev:\n                      prev[nxt] = cur\n                      q.append(nxt)\n      raise RuntimeError(\"No reachable goal cell found.\")\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 1. Identify the goal (stick) and its primitive requirements\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]          # index of the goal item\n  primitive_requirements = cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n  # primitive_requirements: {primitive_idx: count, ...}\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 2. Determine static information about the world layout\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid                               # (W, H, n_kinds)\n  W, H, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Cells that are blocked for movement: any non\u2011zero entry that is *not*\n  # a primitive (i.e. belongs to the set of non\u2011grabbable entities).\n  # ``env.world.non_grabbable_indices`` holds the set of such indices.\n  blocked = np.zeros((W, H), dtype=bool)\n  for idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      blocked |= grid[:, :, idx] > 0\n  # The agent can walk on empty cells and on cells that contain primitives\n  # (they are pick\u2011up-able) \u2013 we treat those as walkable.\n  walkable = ~blocked\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 3. Plan actions to collect each required primitive\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  actions = []\n  cur_pos = state.pos  # (x, y)\n\n  for prim_idx, count in primitive_requirements.items():\n      # locate *all* cells that currently contain this primitive\n      prim_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n      prim_cells = [tuple(c) for c in prim_cells]\n\n      if not prim_cells:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Primitive {cookbook.index.get(prim_idx, prim_idx)} \"\n                             \"not present in the current grid.\")\n\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # Find the nearest instance of the primitive\n          path = bfs(cur_pos, set(prim_cells), walkable)\n\n          # Convert the path (list of positions) into movement actions\n          for (x0, y0), (x1, y1) in zip([cur_pos] + path[:-1], path):\n              dx, dy = x1 - x0, y1 - y0\n              actions.append(DIR_TO_ACTION[(dx, dy)])\n              cur_pos = (x1, y1)\n\n          # At the primitive location we issue a USE action to pick it up\n          actions.append(4)  # USE\n          # After picking up, the primitive disappears from the grid; we\n          # update our local view so that future path\u2011finding does not treat\n          # it as an obstacle.\n          grid[cur_pos[0], cur_pos[1], prim_idx] = 0\n\n          # Remove the used cell from the list (if multiple of the same\n          # primitive are required we may need to come back to another cell)\n          prim_cells = [c for c in prim_cells if c != cur_pos]\n\n          # If we still need more of this primitive but have exhausted the\n          # known cells, we raise an error \u2013 in a well\u2011formed scenario this\n          # should not happen.\n          if not prim_cells and _ < count - 1:\n              raise RuntimeError(\"Not enough instances of required primitive.\")\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 4. Move to the appropriate workshop and craft the stick\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # The workshop name is stored under the special key \"_at\" in the recipe.\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx]\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # Locate the workshop cell(s) \u2013 there should be at least one.\n  workshop_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n  if len(workshop_cells) == 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(f\"Workshop '{workshop_name}' not found in the grid.\")\n  # Choose the closest workshop cell\n  workshop_cells = [tuple(c) for c in workshop_cells]\n  path = bfs(cur_pos, set(workshop_cells), walkable)\n\n  for (x0, y0), (x1, y1) in zip([cur_pos] + path[:-1], path):\n      dx, dy = x1 - x0, y1 - y0\n      actions.append(DIR_TO_ACTION[(dx, dy)])\n      cur_pos = (x1, y1)\n\n  # Final USE to craft the stick\n  actions.append(4)  # USE\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:25:58.800093", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:26:04.548579", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a sequence of actions to complete the task of making a stick in the given environment.\n  The function discovers the required primitives from the recipe for 'stick' and then crafts the stick.\n  Args:\n      env: The environment instance.\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of action indices the agent can execute to complete the task of making a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Identify the index for the stick item\n  stick_index = env.world.cookbook.index(\"stick\")\n  # Get the primitive requirements for a stick\n  stick_primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_index)\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # Gather each required primitive\n  for primitive, count in stick_primitives.items():\n      # Find the location(s) of the primitive in the grid\n      primitive_positions = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n\n      # Collect the required number of each primitive\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # Choose the nearest primitive location\n          agent_pos = np.array(env._current_state.pos)\n          distances = np.linalg.norm(primitive_positions - agent_pos, axis=1)\n          nearest_idx = np.argmin(distances)\n          target_pos = tuple(primitive_positions[nearest_idx])\n\n          # Move to the target position (simple Manhattan path)\n          while env._current_state.pos != target_pos:\n              cur_x, cur_y = env._current_state.pos\n              tar_x, tar_y = target_pos\n\n              if cur_x < tar_x:\n                  actions.append(env.world.n_actions.DOWN)   # Move down\n              elif cur_x > tar_x:\n                  actions.append(env.world.n_actions.UP)     # Move up\n              elif cur_y < tar_y:\n                  actions.append(env.world.n_actions.RIGHT) # Move right\n              elif cur_y > tar_y:\n                  actions.append(env.world.n_actions.LEFT)  # Move left\n\n              # Execute the move to update the internal state\n              _, _ = env.step(actions[-1])\n\n          # Use action to collect the primitive\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions.USE)\n          _, _ = env.step(actions[-1])\n\n          # Remove the collected primitive location\n          primitive_positions = np.delete(primitive_positions, nearest_idx, axis=0)\n\n  # Move to the workshop for crafting sticks (assume workshop is at position with the stick's _at index)\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.recipes[stick_index][\"_at\"]\n  workshop_positions = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, workshop_index] > 0)\n\n  if workshop_positions.size > 0:\n      workshop_pos = tuple(workshop_positions[0])\n      while env._current_state.pos != workshop_pos:\n          cur_x, cur_y = env._current_state.pos\n          tar_x, tar_y = workshop_pos\n\n          if cur_x < tar_x:\n              actions.append(env.world.n_actions.DOWN)\n          elif cur_x > tar_x:\n              actions.append(env.world.n_actions.UP)\n          elif cur_y < tar_y:\n              actions.append(env.world.n_actions.RIGHT)\n          elif cur_y > tar_y:\n              actions.append(env.world.n_actions.LEFT)\n\n          _, _ = env.step(actions[-1])\n\n  # Finally, use the workshop to craft the stick\n  actions.append(env.world.n_actions.USE)\n  _, _ = env.step(actions[-1])\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
