{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:26:23.283873", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a simple action sequence that collects the required primitives for a\n  ``stick`` and then crafts it at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  This implementation makes a number of simplifying assumptions:\n  * The environment follows the ``CraftWorld`` API described in the prompt.\n  * Action indices follow the mapping: DOWN\u21920, UP\u21921, LEFT\u21922, RIGHT\u21923, USE\u21924.\n  * The grid is static (i.e., primitives do not move) and the agent can move\n    freely through empty cells.\n  * There is at least one instance of each required primitive and of the\n    required workshop on the map.\n\n  The function works by:\n  1. Looking up the index of the ``stick`` item.\n  2. Querying the recipe to obtain required primitive kinds and the workshop\n     index (``_at`` entry).\n  3. For each required primitive, moving to the first available cell that\n     contains it and issuing a ``USE`` action to pick it up.\n  4. Finally moving to a workshop cell and issuing ``USE`` to craft the stick.\n\n  The returned list can be fed directly to ``env.step`` in a loop.\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper: translate a Manhattan move into actions.\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def move_to(cur_pos, target_pos, action_list):\n      \"\"\"\n      Append actions that move from ``cur_pos`` to ``target_pos`` using\n      Manhattan (grid) moves.  The function mutates ``action_list`` and returns\n      the new position.\n      \"\"\"\n      x, y = cur_pos\n      tx, ty = target_pos\n\n      # Move in x direction (columns) \u2013 LEFT/RIGHT\n      while x < tx:\n          action_list.append(3)   # RIGHT\n          x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          action_list.append(2)   # LEFT\n          x -= 1\n\n      # Move in y direction (rows) \u2013 DOWN/UP\n      while y < ty:\n          action_list.append(0)   # DOWN\n          y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          action_list.append(1)   # UP\n          y -= 1\n\n      return (x, y)\n\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Identify the stick index and its recipe.\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world\n  scenario = env.scenario\n\n  # Index of the target item (stick)\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n\n  # Full recipe dictionary for the stick (may contain \"_at\" entry)\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n\n  # Separate primitive requirements from the special keys (e.g., \"_at\")\n  primitive_reqs = {k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if not k.startswith(\"_\")}\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\")  # workshop where crafting must occur\n\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Locate all entities on the static initial grid.\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  grid = scenario.init_grid  # shape (W, H, n_kinds)\n  # Current agent position (start)\n  cur_pos = tuple(scenario.init_pos)\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Collect each required primitive.\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_reqs.items():\n      # Find all cells that currently contain this primitive.\n      prim_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n\n      # Simple strategy: take the first ``needed`` cells (no path planning).\n      for i in range(needed):\n          if i >= len(prim_cells):\n              # Not enough primitives on the map \u2013 abort early.\n              break\n          target = tuple(prim_cells[i])\n          # Move to the primitive location.\n          cur_pos = move_to(cur_pos, target, actions)\n          # Pick it up.\n          actions.append(4)   # USE\n          # After collection, we could update the grid to reflect the removal,\n          # but for the purpose of generating a static action list it is not\n          # required.\n\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Move to the workshop and craft the stick.\n  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      workshop_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n      if len(workshop_cells) > 0:\n          target = tuple(workshop_cells[0])\n          cur_pos = move_to(cur_pos, target, actions)\n          actions.append(4)   # USE to craft\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
