{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:32:52.121895", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  # Resolve index for stick\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      return []\n  # Get primitive requirements\n  try:\n      primitive_requirements = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n  except Exception:\n      primitive_requirements = {}\n  # Use environment planning helper if available\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan_to_craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.plan_to_craft(stick_idx, primitive_requirements)\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n  # Fallback: try direct craft method\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.craft(\"stick\")\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n  # No plan possible\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:33:03.537422", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of low\u2011level action indices that will cause the agent to\n  obtain at least one ``stick`` in the supplied CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation is deliberately generic: it queries the world\u2019s\n  ``Cookbook`` for the index and primitive requirements of a stick and\n  then asks the environment (if possible) for a concrete plan.  If the\n  environment does not expose a planning helper we fall back to any\n  available ``craft`` method; otherwise an empty plan is returned.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the CraftWorld environment (or a compatible mock).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      Sequence of action indices that achieve the goal.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Resolve the integer index for the goal item ``stick``.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:  # Defensive fallback if world/cookbook missing\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Determine which primitive resources are required to craft a stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  try:\n      primitive_requirements = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n  except Exception:\n      primitive_requirements = {}\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Ask the environment for a concrete plan, if it provides one.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  plan = []\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan_to_craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.plan_to_craft(stick_idx, primitive_requirements)\n      except Exception:\n          plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Fallback: use a direct ``craft`` helper if available.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  elif hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          # ``craft`` may accept either the name or the index.\n          plan = env.craft(\"stick\")\n      except Exception:\n          plan = []\n\n  # Ensure a list of ints is returned.\n  return list(plan)", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
