{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:36:21.969236", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that would allow the agent to craft a *stick*.\n\n  The function follows a very simple (and safe) strategy:\n  1. Identify the index of the ``stick`` item using the world's cookbook.\n  2. Query the cookbook for the primitive resources required to craft a stick.\n  3. For each required primitive, locate the nearest cell that contains it.\n     (If the primitive cannot be found, the function simply skips it.)\n  4. Move the agent towards that cell using Manhattan moves (UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT)\n     and issue a ``USE`` action to pick up the primitive.\n  5. Once all required primitives have been collected, move to a workshop that\n     can craft the stick (the workshop type is stored in the recipe under the\n     ``_at`` key) and issue a final ``USE`` action to perform the crafting.\n\n  Because the exact layout of the grid and the positions of primitives /\n  workshops are environment\u2011specific, the implementation performs a\n  breadth\u2011first search on the current grid to find the shortest path to each\n  target.  The returned list contains integer action IDs that match the\n  ``CraftLab`` action specification (0\u2011DOWN, 1\u2011UP, 2\u2011LEFT, 3\u2011RIGHT, 4\u2011USE).\n\n  If any step fails (e.g., a required primitive is not present), the function\n  simply returns the actions accumulated up to that point.  This makes the\n  implementation robust and ensures it always returns a valid list of actions.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : CraftLab\n      The environment instance providing access to the world, current state,\n      and action space.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially in the\n      environment, will result in the agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper functions\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def bfs(start, target_kind):\n      \"\"\"Breadth\u2011first search returning a list of actions to reach a cell\n      containing ``target_kind``.  Returns None if unreachable.\"\"\"\n      from collections import deque\n\n      # Directions: (dy, dx, action_id)\n      dirs = [(-1, 0, 1), (1, 0, 0), (0, -1, 2), (0, 1, 3)]\n\n      visited = set()\n      queue = deque()\n      queue.append((start, []))\n      visited.add(start)\n\n      while queue:\n          (y, x), actions = queue.popleft()\n          # Check current cell for the target kind\n          if state.grid[y, x, target_kind] > 0:\n              return actions\n          # Expand neighbours\n          for dy, dx, act in dirs:\n              ny, nx = y + dy, x + dx\n              if 0 <= ny < state.grid.shape[0] and 0 <= nx < state.grid.shape[1]:\n                  if (ny, nx) not in visited:\n                      # cell must be traversable (no non\u2011grabbable entity)\n                      blocked = any(\n                          state.grid[ny, nx, idx] > 0\n                          for idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n                      )\n                      if not blocked:\n                          visited.add((ny, nx))\n                          queue.append(((ny, nx), actions + [act]))\n      return None\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Main logic\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n\n  # Current state object\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # 1. Identify the index for \"stick\"\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except KeyError:\n      # No stick defined in the cookbook \u2013 nothing to do.\n      return actions\n\n  # 2. Determine required primitives for a stick\n  prim_dict = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # 3. Gather each primitive\n  for prim_idx, count in prim_dict.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # Find path to the nearest cell containing this primitive\n          path = bfs(state.pos, prim_idx)\n          if path is None:\n              # Primitive not reachable \u2013 abort further collection\n              return actions\n          actions.extend(path)\n          # Use action to pick up the primitive\n          actions.append(4)  # USE\n          # Simulate the steps locally to keep ``state`` in sync\n          for a in path:\n              state = state.step(a)[1]  # ignore reward\n          state = state.step(4)[1]\n\n  # 4. Move to the appropriate workshop (if any)\n  workshop_kind = None\n  # The recipe may contain an \"_at\" entry specifying the workshop type\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_name:\n      workshop_kind = env.world.cookbook.index.get(workshop_name)\n  if workshop_kind is not None:\n      path = bfs(state.pos, workshop_kind)\n      if path is not None:\n          actions.extend(path)\n          for a in path:\n              state = state.step(a)[1]\n          # Finally, craft the stick at the workshop\n          actions.append(4)  # USE\n          state = state.step(4)[1]\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
