{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T17:55:27.064843", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given\n  CraftWorld environment.  The function works for any environment that\n  follows the DMLab\u2011style interface used by the ``CraftLab`` wrapper.\n\n  The algorithm is simple:\n    1.  Look up the index of the ``stick`` item in the cookbook.\n    2.  Retrieve the primitive requirements for a single stick.\n    3.  For each required primitive, locate a cell that contains the\n        primitive, move the agent next to that cell and ``USE`` to pick\n        it up (repeating until the required count is satisfied).\n    4.  Locate the workshop where a stick can be crafted (the ``_at``\n        entry of the recipe), move next to it and ``USE`` to craft the\n        stick.\n\n  The function does **not** execute the actions \u2013 it only returns the\n  list of integer actions that can later be fed to ``env.step``.\n  The implementation is deliberately straightforward and does not\n  attempt sophisticated path\u2011finding; it simply walks Manhattan\u2011style\n  towards the target coordinates.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : CraftLab\n      An instance of the CraftLab environment (already reset).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed in order, will\n      result in at least one ``stick`` in the agent's inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper constants \u2013 action indices used by CraftLab\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper functions for movement and interaction\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def manhattan_move(cur_pos, target_pos):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of actions that move from cur_pos to target_pos.\"\"\"\n      x, y = cur_pos\n      tx, ty = target_pos\n      actions = []\n      # first move in x direction\n      while x < tx:\n          actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n          x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          actions.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n          x -= 1\n      # then move in y direction\n      while y < ty:\n          actions.append(ACTION_DOWN)\n          y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          actions.append(ACTION_UP)\n          y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Access to world data\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world                     # CraftWorld instance\n  cookbook = world.cookbook             # Cookbook instance\n  state = env._current_state            # CraftState instance\n  grid = state.grid                      # (W, H, n_kinds) array\n  pos = tuple(state.pos)                # (x, y)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Identify the stick item and its recipe\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # The recipe dict contains primitive indices and a special key \"_at\"\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Determine which workshop is required for crafting the stick\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  workshop_name = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Determine primitive requirements (exclude the special \"_at\" key)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  primitive_requirements = {\n      i_kind: cnt\n      for i_kind, cnt in recipe.items()\n      if i_kind != \"_at\"\n  }\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Action list we will build and return\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  action_plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper to locate a cell containing a given kind (any occurrence)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def locate_kind(kind):\n      \"\"\"Return coordinates (x, y) of any cell that contains `kind`.\"\"\"\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind] > 0)\n      if len(locations) == 0:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot find required kind {kind} in the grid.\")\n      # pick the first location (could be improved)\n      return tuple(locations[0][:2])\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Collect each required primitive\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_requirements.items():\n      while state.inventory[prim_idx] < needed:\n          # locate a source cell for this primitive\n          src_x, src_y = locate_kind(prim_idx)\n\n          # move next to the source cell (we stand on the same cell)\n          # the USE action works on the cell we are standing on.\n          moves = manhattan_move(pos, (src_x, src_y))\n          action_plan.extend(moves)\n          pos = (src_x, src_y)\n\n          # pick up the primitive\n          action_plan.append(ACTION_USE)\n\n          # simulate the effect locally so we know our next position /\n          # inventory without having to query the environment.\n          # This is cheap because we only need the inventory count.\n          # (In a real run the environment would update these.)\n          state.inventory[prim_idx] += 1\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Move to the workshop and craft the stick\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # locate any workshop cell of the required type\n  ws_x, ws_y = locate_kind(workshop_idx)\n\n  # move next to the workshop\n  moves = manhattan_move(pos, (ws_x, ws_y))\n  action_plan.extend(moves)\n  pos = (ws_x, ws_y)\n\n  # craft the stick\n  action_plan.append(ACTION_USE)\n\n  return action_plan", "env_interactions": 4, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
