{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:02:11.239051", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that will collect the required primitives\n  for a stick and craft it at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  The implementation is generic and works for any CraftWorld environment\n  that follows the schema described in the prompt. It:\n    1. Looks up the integer index for the item named ``\"stick\"``.\n    2. Retrieves the primitive requirements for one stick via\n       ``world.cookbook.primitives_for``.\n    3. For each required primitive it finds the nearest cell that contains\n       that primitive and generates Manhattan\u2011movement actions to reach it,\n       followed by a ``USE`` action to pick it up.\n    4. After all primitives are collected it moves to the workshop specified\n       by the recipe (the ``\"_at\"`` entry) and performs a final ``USE`` to\n       craft the stick.\n\n  The function returns the list of action indices; it does **not** execute\n  them.  It assumes that the action constants are defined in the ``craft``\n  module (e.g. ``craft.DOWN``, ``craft.UP``, ``craft.LEFT``, ``craft.RIGHT``,\n  ``craft.USE``).  If any of the required entities are missing from the grid,\n  the planner simply skips them \u2013 the returned plan will still be a valid\n  list of actions, albeit possibly incomplete.\n\n  Args:\n      env: An instance of ``CraftLab`` (or any wrapper that exposes the same\n           attributes used below).  The function accesses ``env.world``,\n           ``env._current_state`` and the ``craft`` module for action\n           constants.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of action indices that, when executed in order,\n                 should result in the agent possessing at least one stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n  from craft import craft  # action constants\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper: Manhattan\u2011distance movement planner\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def plan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Yield a list of movement actions (DOWN/UP/RIGHT/LEFT) from start to goal.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      cur = list(start)\n      # vertical moves (row index)\n      while cur[0] < goal[0]:\n          actions.append(craft.DOWN)\n          cur[0] += 1\n      while cur[0] > goal[0]:\n          actions.append(craft.UP)\n          cur[0] -= 1\n      # horizontal moves (col index)\n      while cur[1] < goal[1]:\n          actions.append(craft.RIGHT)\n          cur[1] += 1\n      while cur[1] > goal[1]:\n          actions.append(craft.LEFT)\n          cur[1] -= 1\n      return actions, tuple(cur)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Access world, state and recipe information\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world\n  state = env._current_state\n  grid = state.grid  # shape (W, H, n_kinds)\n  pos = state.pos    # (row, col)\n\n  # Index of the target item \"stick\"\n  try:\n      stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      # If the name is not present, we cannot plan; return empty plan.\n      return []\n\n  # Primitive requirements for a single stick (may be empty if stick is primitive)\n  primitive_requirements = world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  plan = []  # accumulated action list\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Collect each required primitive the needed number of times\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed_cnt in primitive_requirements.items():\n      for _ in range(needed_cnt):\n          # Find all grid cells that currently contain the primitive\n          locations = np.argwhere(grid[..., prim_idx] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              # No instance on the map \u2013 skip (plan will be incomplete)\n              continue\n          # Choose the nearest location (Manhattan distance)\n          dists = np.sum(np.abs(locations - np.array(pos)), axis=1)\n          target_loc = locations[np.argmin(dists)]\n          # Move to the primitive\n          moves, pos = plan_path(pos, tuple(target_loc))\n          plan.extend(moves)\n          # Pick it up\n          plan.append(craft.USE)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Move to the workshop for the stick and craft it\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The recipe dict contains an \"_at\" key that specifies the workshop kind\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_kind = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n  if workshop_kind is not None:\n      # Locate all workshop cells of the required kind\n      workshop_cells = np.argwhere(grid[..., workshop_kind] > 0)\n      if workshop_cells.size > 0:\n          dists = np.sum(np.abs(workshop_cells - np.array(pos)), axis=1)\n          workshop_target = workshop_cells[np.argmin(dists)]\n          moves, pos = plan_path(pos, tuple(workshop_target))\n          plan.extend(moves)\n          # Craft the stick\n          plan.append(craft.USE)\n\n  return plan", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
