{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:19:16.431795", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of actions that makes the agent craft a ``stick`` in the\n  provided ``CraftLab`` environment.\n\n  The implementation is completely generic \u2013 it works for any\n  ``CraftWorld`` configuration as long as a recipe for ``stick`` exists.\n  The steps are:\n\n  1.  Locate the index of the item ``stick`` in the world\u2019s ``Cookbook``.\n  2.  Ask the ``Cookbook`` for the primitive requirements of that item.\n  3.  For each required primitive:\n      *   Find the *nearest* cell that currently holds the primitive.\n      *   Move the agent to that cell (using Manhattan moves).\n      *   Issue a ``USE`` action to pick the primitive up.\n  4.  After all primitives are in the inventory, move to a workshop that\n      can craft ``stick`` (the workshop type is stored in the recipe under\n      the special key ``\"_at\"``) and issue a final ``USE`` to craft it.\n\n  The function does **not** execute the actions \u2013 it only returns the\n  integer action sequence.  The caller can feed the list to ``env.step``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Helper constants \u2013 they match the action ordering used by CraftWorld. #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Helper utilities.                                                   #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  def manhattan_path(src, dst):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of moves (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that walks from src to dst.\"\"\"\n      sx, sy = src\n      dx, dy = dst\n      moves = []\n      # vertical movement\n      while sx < dx:\n          moves.append(DOWN)\n          sx += 1\n      while sx > dx:\n          moves.append(UP)\n          sx -= 1\n      # horizontal movement\n      while sy < dy:\n          moves.append(RIGHT)\n          sy += 1\n      while sy > dy:\n          moves.append(LEFT)\n          sy -= 1\n      return moves\n\n  def nearest_position(grid, kind_idx, start_pos):\n      \"\"\"Find the nearest cell (Manhattan distance) that contains ``kind_idx``.\"\"\"\n      h, w = grid.shape[:2]\n      best = None\n      best_dist = None\n      # ``grid`` is (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n      for x in range(w):\n          for y in range(h):\n              if grid[x, y, kind_idx] > 0:\n                  dist = abs(x - start_pos[0]) + abs(y - start_pos[1])\n                  if best_dist is None or dist < best_dist:\n                      best_dist = dist\n                      best = (x, y)\n      return best\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 1.  Resolve the index of ``stick``.                                   #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index['stick']           # raises KeyError if not present\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 2.  Primitive requirements for the recipe.                           #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns a dict {primitive_idx: count}.\n  primitive_needs = cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # The workshop where the stick must be crafted is stored under the key\n  # ``\"_at\"`` in the recipe dict.\n  workshop_kind = cookbook.recipes[stick_idx].get('_at', None)\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 3.  Reset the environment to obtain a fresh state.                    #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # ``env.reset`` returns an observation dict \u2013 we only need the internal\n  # state to read the grid and the agent\u2019s position.\n  env.reset()\n  state = env._current_state          # type: CraftState\n  actions = []\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 4.  Collect every required primitive.                                 #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  for prim_idx, count in primitive_needs.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # locate the nearest instance of the primitive\n          target = nearest_position(state.grid, prim_idx, state.pos)\n          if target is None:\n              raise RuntimeError(f\"Primitive {prim_idx} not found on the map.\")\n          # move to the primitive\n          actions += manhattan_path(state.pos, target)\n          # pick it up\n          actions.append(USE)\n          # simulate the move locally so that subsequent searches use the\n          # updated position (the environment itself will also move when the\n          # actions are executed by the caller).\n          state.pos = target\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 5.  Move to the appropriate workshop and craft the stick.            #\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  if workshop_kind is not None:\n      workshop_pos = nearest_position(state.grid, workshop_kind, state.pos)\n      if workshop_pos is None:\n          raise RuntimeError(\"No workshop of the required type found on the map.\")\n      actions += manhattan_path(state.pos, workshop_pos)\n      actions.append(USE)   # craft at the workshop\n  else:\n      # If the recipe does not require a workshop we can simply USE at the\n      # current location.\n      actions.append(USE)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
