{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:30:00.684388", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that will cause the agent to craft a ``stick``.\n  The implementation works with the generic CraftWorld API exposed by the\n  ``env`` object (which contains a ``state`` attribute of type ``CraftState``).\n\n  The algorithm is straightforward:\n  1.  Query the recipe for ``stick`` via the world\u2019s ``Cookbook``.\n  2.  For each required primitive, locate the nearest cell that contains it,\n      walk to that cell and ``USE`` it (collecting the item).\n  3.  After all primitives are in the inventory, locate any workshop that can\n      craft a stick, walk to it and ``USE`` again to perform the crafting.\n  4.  Return the concatenated list of actions.\n\n  The function makes no assumptions about the exact layout of the world \u2013\n  it simply uses Manhattan distance to decide a greedy (but sufficient)\n  path.  The action indices follow the convention used throughout the\n  CraftWorld code base:\n\n      0 \u2192 DOWN\n      1 \u2192 UP\n      2 \u2192 LEFT\n      3 \u2192 RIGHT\n      4 \u2192 USE   (collect / craft)\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the CraftWorld environment.  It must expose the\n      attributes ``state`` (a ``CraftState``) and ``world`` (a ``CraftWorld``).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A sequence of action indices that, when executed in order, will result\n      in at least one ``stick`` in the agent\u2019s inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_UP, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  def manhattan(a, b):\n      return abs(a[0] - b[0]) + abs(a[1] - b[1])\n\n  def greedy_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Yield a list of movement actions that walk from ``start`` to ``goal``.\"\"\"\n      x, y = start\n      gx, gy = goal\n      actions = []\n      # move in x direction\n      while x != gx:\n          if gx > x:\n              actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n              x += 1\n          else:\n              actions.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n              x -= 1\n      # move in y direction\n      while y != gy:\n          if gy > y:\n              actions.append(ACTION_DOWN)\n              y += 1\n          else:\n              actions.append(ACTION_UP)\n              y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 1. Identify the goal index for \u201cstick\u201d and its recipe.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  stick_name = \"stick\"\n  # The Index object maps names \u2192 integer IDs.\n  stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[stick_name]\n  if stick_idx is None:\n      raise ValueError(f\"Stick not found in the cookbook (name = '{stick_name}').\")\n\n  # Primitive requirements for one stick.\n  primitive_requirements = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)  # {prim_idx: count}\n  if not primitive_requirements:\n      # No recipe \u2013 stick must be a primitive itself.  In that case we only need\n      # to pick it up if it exists on the map.\n      primitive_requirements = {stick_idx: 1}\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 2. Collect all required primitives.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  actions = []\n  grid = env.state.grid           # shape (W, H, n_kinds)\n  pos = tuple(env.state.pos)      # (x, y)\n  inventory = env.state.inventory.copy()\n\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_requirements.items():\n      while inventory[prim_idx] < needed:\n          # Locate the nearest cell that still contains this primitive.\n          # ``grid[..., prim_idx]`` is a 2\u2011D boolean/int mask of where the\n          # primitive exists.\n          locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              raise RuntimeError(f\"Required primitive (idx={prim_idx}) not present on the map.\")\n          # Choose the location with minimal Manhattan distance.\n          dists = np.apply_along_axis(lambda loc: manhattan(pos, (loc[0], loc[1])),\n                                      1, locations)\n          nearest = locations[np.argmin(dists)]\n          target = (int(nearest[0]), int(nearest[1]))\n\n          # Walk to the target cell.\n          actions.extend(greedy_path(pos, target))\n          pos = target\n\n          # Collect the primitive.\n          actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n          # Simulate the effect on the local copy of state so that subsequent\n          # steps see the updated inventory and grid.\n          # Remove one instance from the grid.\n          grid[pos[0], pos[1], prim_idx] -= 1\n          inventory[prim_idx] += 1\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 3. Move to a workshop that can craft a stick and perform the craft.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # The recipe dict stored in ``Cookbook.recipes`` contains a special key\n  # \"_at\" indicating the workshop type required for the output.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_type = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_type is None:\n      # No specific workshop \u2013 the craft can be performed anywhere.\n      # We simply invoke USE at the current location.\n      actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n      return actions\n\n  # Convert workshop name to its index.\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_type]\n  # Find any cell that contains this workshop.\n  workshop_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n  if workshop_cells.size == 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(f\"No workshop of type '{workshop_type}' found on the map.\")\n\n  # Choose the nearest workshop.\n  dists = np.apply_along_axis(lambda loc: manhattan(pos, (loc[0], loc[1])),\n                              1, workshop_cells)\n  nearest_ws = workshop_cells[np.argmin(dists)]\n  ws_target = (int(nearest_ws[0]), int(nearest_ws[1]))\n\n  # Walk to the workshop.\n  actions.extend(greedy_path(pos, ws_target))\n  pos = ws_target\n\n  # Craft the stick.\n  actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
