{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:33:47.907775", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a list of actions that will cause the agent to craft a stick in the\n  provided CraftWorld environment.\n  The function first tries to use a built\u2011in planner (env.plan).  If the\n  planner is not present it falls back to a very simple heuristic:\n  it repeatedly executes the USE action (env.action_space['USE'] or 4)\n  while moving randomly until a stick appears in the inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n  # try planner\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.plan(\"stick\")\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  # determine action indices\n  try:\n      use_action = env.action_space[\"USE\"]\n  except Exception:\n      # fallback to typical index 4\n      use_action = 4\n  # try moving actions\n  move_actions = [0,1,2,3]  # DOWN,UP,LEFT,RIGHT typical order\n  actions = []\n  # simple loop limited steps\n  max_steps = 200\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # attempt to use (collect/craft)\n      actions.append(use_action)\n      # check if goal satisfied via env observation?\n      # if env has method 'has_item' we can query, else break after max_steps\n      if hasattr(env, \"has_item\"):\n          if env.has_item(\"stick\"):\n              break\n      # move randomly\n      actions.append(np.random.choice(move_actions))\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
