{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:36:40.281494", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that allows the agent to craft a ``stick``.\n  The plan is simple:\n    1.  Determine which primitive items are required for a stick and where they are.\n    2.  Move to each primitive, use the ``USE`` action to pick it up.\n    3.  Move to the required workshop and ``USE`` again to craft the stick.\n\n  The implementation assumes the environment has already been reset, i.e. it\n  possesses a ``_current_state`` attribute of type :class:`CraftState`.  The\n  action ordering follows the specification in ``CraftLab.action_specs``:\n      0 \u2013 DOWN, 1 \u2013 UP, 2 \u2013 LEFT, 3 \u2013 RIGHT, 4 \u2013 USE\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Helper: generate a Manhattan\u2011style path from ``src`` to ``dst``.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  def _move_path(src, dst):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of actions (DOWN/UP/LEFT/RIGHT) that moves from src to dst.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      x, y = src\n      tx, ty = dst\n      # vertical moves (DOWN = 0, UP = 1)\n      while x < tx:\n          actions.append(0)   # DOWN\n          x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          actions.append(1)   # UP\n          x -= 1\n      # horizontal moves (LEFT = 2, RIGHT = 3)\n      while y < ty:\n          actions.append(3)   # RIGHT\n          y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          actions.append(2)   # LEFT\n          y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 1.  Locate the indices for ``stick`` and its recipe.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      # No ``stick`` defined \u2013 nothing to do.\n      return []\n\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  # Primitive requirements (ignore the special keys ``_key`` and ``_at``)\n  primitive_reqs = {k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if k not in (\"_key\", \"_at\")}\n  # Workshop where the stick must be crafted\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_name is None:\n      # No workshop information \u2013 cannot craft.\n      return []\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 2.  Gather current state information.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  state = env._current_state          # type: CraftState\n  grid = state.grid                    # shape (W, H, n_kinds)\n  pos = state.pos                      # (x, y)\n\n  actions_plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 3.  Collect each required primitive the necessary number of times.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_reqs.items():\n      for _ in range(needed):\n          # Find any cell that still contains the primitive.\n          locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              # Primitive not present \u2013 give up (return what we have).\n              return actions_plan\n          target = tuple(locations[0])   # pick the first occurrence\n\n          # Move to the primitive.\n          actions_plan.extend(_move_path(pos, target))\n          pos = target\n\n          # Pick it up.\n          actions_plan.append(4)          # USE\n          # Simulate removal from the grid so we don't try to pick the same\n          # instance again (optional, but keeps the planner consistent).\n          grid[pos[0], pos[1], prim_idx] = 0\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 4.  Move to the required workshop and craft the stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  workshop_locs = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n  if workshop_locs.size == 0:\n      # No workshop found \u2013 cannot finish the plan.\n      return actions_plan\n  workshop_pos = tuple(workshop_locs[0])\n\n  actions_plan.extend(_move_path(pos, workshop_pos))\n  # Final USE to craft the stick.\n  actions_plan.append(4)\n\n  return actions_plan", "env_interactions": 4, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:37:27.530937", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  The implementation first tries to use a built\u2011in planner (if the environment\n  provides a ``plan`` method) and falls back to an empty action list if no\n  planner is available or if planning fails.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Use the environment's planner if it exists.\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan\"):\n      try:\n          # ``env.plan`` is expected to return an iterable of action indices.\n          return list(env.plan(\"stick\"))\n      except Exception:\n          # If planning fails for any reason we simply fall back.\n          pass\n\n  # Fallback: no actions (the caller may handle this case).\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
