{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:42:27.895446", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a sequence of actions that makes a stick in the given CraftLab\n  environment. The algorithm is a very simple planner:\n    1. Query the world recipe for ``stick`` to obtain the required primitive\n       items and their counts.\n    2. Repeatedly locate each needed primitive in the grid, move the agent\n       to the cell, and ``USE`` (action 4) to pick it up.\n    3. Locate the workshop required for the ``stick`` recipe, move the\n       agent there and ``USE`` to craft the stick.\n\n  The function works with the public API of ``CraftLab`` and the internal\n  ``CraftState`` representation.  It assumes the following action encoding\n  (as defined in ``CraftLab.action_specs``):\n\n      0: DOWN   (y + 1)\n      1: UP     (y - 1)\n      2: LEFT   (x - 1)\n      3: RIGHT  (x + 1)\n      4: USE    (collect / craft)\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : CraftLab\n      The environment instance (already reset).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially, will\n      result in the agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def manhattan_step(pos, target):\n      \"\"\"Return a single movement action that brings ``pos`` one step closer\n      to ``target`` (ignoring obstacles).\"\"\"\n      x, y = pos\n      tx, ty = target\n      if x < tx:\n          return 3      # RIGHT\n      if x > tx:\n          return 2      # LEFT\n      if y < ty:\n          return 0      # DOWN\n      if y > ty:\n          return 1      # UP\n      # already at target \u2013 no movement needed\n      return None\n\n  def locate_item(grid, kind_idx):\n      \"\"\"Return the (x, y) coordinate of any cell that contains ``kind_idx``.\n      If the item is not present, return None.\"\"\"\n      # grid shape: (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n      # we look for any non\u2011zero entry in the slice grid[:, :, kind_idx]\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind_idx] > 0)\n      if locations.size == 0:\n          return None\n      # take the first found location\n      return tuple(locations[0].tolist())\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Access world/cookbook information\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world                      # CraftWorld instance\n  state = env._current_state             # CraftState instance\n  grid = state.grid.copy()               # current grid occupancy\n  pos = tuple(state.pos)                 # (x, y) current position\n  # ``stick`` name is fixed in the recipes; obtain its index\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # primitives needed for a single stick (primitive_idx -> count)\n  primitives = world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  actions = []  # the action sequence we will build\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Collect all required primitives\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitives.items():\n      # count how many of this primitive we have already\n      have = int(state.inventory[prim_idx])\n      while have < needed:\n          # locate a cell that still contains the primitive\n          target = locate_item(grid, prim_idx)\n          if target is None:\n              # No more of this primitive on the map \u2013 abort (cannot craft)\n              raise RuntimeError(\"Required primitive not found on the grid.\")\n          # Move step\u2011by\u2011step towards the target\n          while pos != target:\n              act = manhattan_step(pos, target)\n              if act is None:\n                  break\n              actions.append(act)\n              # simulate the move to keep ``pos`` in sync with the actions\n              if act == 0:   # DOWN\n                  pos = (pos[0], pos[1] + 1)\n              elif act == 1: # UP\n                  pos = (pos[0], pos[1] - 1)\n              elif act == 2: # LEFT\n                  pos = (pos[0] - 1, pos[1])\n              elif act == 3: # RIGHT\n                  pos = (pos[0] + 1, pos[1])\n              # NOTE: we do *not* update ``grid`` here \u2013 the environment will\n              # do it when the action list is actually executed.\n          # We are now adjacent (actually on) the primitive cell.\n          # Use the item\n          actions.append(4)      # USE\n          # Update our internal bookkeeping\n          have += 1\n          state.inventory[prim_idx] += 1\n          # Remove the primitive from our local copy of the grid so we do\n          # not try to collect the same instance again.\n          grid[target[0], target[1], prim_idx] = 0\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Go to the required workshop and craft the stick\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The workshop kind is stored under the special key \"_at\" in the recipe.\n  workshop_kind = world.cookbook.recipes[stick_idx][\"_at\"]\n  workshop_pos = locate_item(grid, workshop_kind)\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n      raise RuntimeError(\"Workshop for stick not found on the grid.\")\n  # Move to the workshop\n  while pos != workshop_pos:\n      act = manhattan_step(pos, workshop_pos)\n      if act is None:\n          break\n      actions.append(act)\n      if act == 0:\n          pos = (pos[0], pos[1] + 1)\n      elif act == 1:\n          pos = (pos[0], pos[1] - 1)\n      elif act == 2:\n          pos = (pos[0] - 1, pos[1])\n      elif act == 3:\n          pos = (pos[0] + 1, pos[1])\n  # Craft the stick\n  actions.append(4)  # USE at the workshop\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
