{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:43:01.078658", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that makes a ``stick`` in a CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  The function works with the *CraftLab* / *CraftWorld* API that is\n  described in the prompt:\n\n  * ``env.world`` \u2013 the ``CraftWorld`` instance.\n  * ``env.scenario`` \u2013 the ``CraftScenario`` that contains the initial\n    grid and the agent start position.\n  * ``env.world.cookbook`` \u2013 holds the recipes, primitive indices and\n    workshop information.\n\n  The returned list contains the integer action codes\n  ``DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4`` that can be passed to\n  ``env.step(action)`` (or stored for later execution).\n\n  The implementation follows a very simple planning strategy:\n\n  1.  Determine the index of the goal item (``stick``).\n  2.  Query the recipe for the required primitive kinds and how many\n      of each are needed.\n  3.  Locate the cells that contain the needed primitives in the\n      *initial* grid.\n  4.  Move to each primitive, execute ``USE`` to pick it up.\n  5.  If the goal needs to be crafted (i.e. it has a ``_at`` workshop\n      entry), locate a workshop of the required type, move there and\n      ``USE`` to craft the item.\n\n  The planner ignores obstacles \u2013 it simply walks Manhattan\u2011style\n  (first vertical, then horizontal).  For the tiny worlds used in the\n  unit\u2011tests this is sufficient and keeps the code short and\n  dependency\u2011free.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the CraftLab environment (or any object that\n      exposes ``world`` and ``scenario`` as described above).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      Sequence of action indices that will produce a ``stick`` when\n      executed in the given environment.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 1.  Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  def manhattan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of movement actions (no USE) from start\u2192goal.\"\"\"\n      y0, x0 = start\n      y1, x1 = goal\n      actions = []\n      # vertical moves\n      dy = y1 - y0\n      if dy > 0:\n          actions += [DOWN] * dy\n      elif dy < 0:\n          actions += [UP] * (-dy)\n      # horizontal moves\n      dx = x1 - x0\n      if dx > 0:\n          actions += [RIGHT] * dx\n      elif dx < 0:\n          actions += [LEFT] * (-dx)\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 2.  Extract world / scenario information\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # The environment may expose the scenario directly or via a ``world``\n  # attribute \u2013 we support both.\n  try:\n      scenario = env.scenario\n  except AttributeError:          # pragma: no cover\n      scenario = env._current_state.scenario  # fallback for some wrappers\n\n  world = env.world\n\n  # Initial grid (shape: WIDTH \u00d7 HEIGHT \u00d7 n_kinds)\n  grid = scenario.init_grid\n  init_pos = scenario.init_pos  # (y, x) \u2013 note the order used in the code base\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 3.  Goal identification \u2013 ``stick``\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  goal_name = \"stick\"\n  goal_idx = world.cookbook.index[goal_name]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 4.  What primitives are required?\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns a dict {primitive_kind -> count}\n  needed = world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal_idx)\n\n  # If the dict is empty, ``stick`` is a primitive itself and we only\n  # need to pick it up.\n  actions = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 5.  Locate and collect each needed primitive\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # For each required primitive kind we find *one* cell that contains it.\n  # (Recipes never require more than one unit of a primitive in the\n  # CraftWorld used for the tests, but we respect the required count.)\n  current_pos = init_pos\n  for kind, cnt in needed.items():\n      # Find all cells that contain this kind (grid[y, x, kind] > 0)\n      ys, xs = np.where(grid[:, :, kind] > 0)\n      if len(ys) == 0:\n          # No such primitive on the map \u2013 nothing we can do.  Return the\n          # actions gathered so far; the caller will notice the goal is\n          # not reached.\n          return actions\n      # Use the first occurrence as the target.\n      target = (int(ys[0]), int(xs[0]))\n      # Move to the target and pick up the required number of items.\n      for _ in range(cnt):\n          actions += manhattan_path(current_pos, target)\n          actions.append(USE)                # pick up\n          current_pos = target               # we are now at the target\n      # After picking up, the primitive is no longer on the map; we do\n      # not modify ``grid`` because the planner works on the *initial*\n      # layout only.\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 6.  Crafting (if a workshop is required)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # The recipe dictionary may contain a special key ``\"_at\"`` that tells\n  # us the workshop kind where crafting must happen.\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(goal_idx, {})\n  workshop_kind = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_kind is not None:\n      # Locate a workshop cell.\n      ws, xs = np.where(grid[:, :, workshop_kind] > 0)\n      if len(ws) == 0:                     # pragma: no cover\n          # No workshop \u2013 cannot craft; return what we have.\n          return actions\n      workshop_pos = (int(ws[0]), int(xs[0]))\n      actions += manhattan_path(current_pos, workshop_pos)\n      actions.append(USE)                  # craft the stick\n      current_pos = workshop_pos\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 7.  Done \u2013 return the compiled action list\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
