{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:55:08.190088", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that (approximately) makes a stick in the given\n  CraftLab environment.\n\n  The implementation follows a very simple heuristic:\n  1. Identify the index of the ``stick`` item in the world cookbook.\n  2. Repeatedly check whether the goal is already satisfied.\n  3. If a required primitive (or the required workshop) is adjacent to the\n     agent, use the ``USE`` action to collect/craft it.\n  4. Otherwise, take a random movement action.\n  5. Stop after a maximum number of steps or when the goal is achieved.\n\n  The function does **not** modify the environment permanently \u2013 it only\n  records the actions it would take.  The returned list can be fed back to\n  ``env.step`` to reproduce the behaviour.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : CraftLab\n      A reset CraftLab environment instance.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of integer action indices that, when executed in order,\n      should result in obtaining at least one ``stick`` in the inventory.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Ensure the environment is in a fresh state.\n  # ``reset`` returns the initial observation dict; we ignore it.\n  env.reset()\n\n  # Mapping from action name to integer index.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()          # e.g. {\"UP\":0, \"DOWN\":1, ...}\n  use_action = action_map[\"USE\"]\n  move_actions = [action_map[d] for d in (\"UP\", \"DOWN\", \"LEFT\", \"RIGHT\")]\n\n  # Index of the goal item (stick) in the world cookbook.\n  stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n\n  # Helper to check if the goal is already satisfied.\n  def goal_reached():\n      # ``satisfies`` expects a name (ignored) and the index of the goal.\n      return env._current_state.satisfies(\"\", stick_idx)\n\n  # Primitive requirements for a single stick.\n  prim_req = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)  # {prim_idx: count}\n  # Workshop kind required for the stick (if any).\n  workshop_kind = None\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  if \"_at\" in recipe:\n      workshop_kind = recipe[\"_at\"]   # this is already an integer kind\n\n  # The sequence of actions we will return.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Simple loop with a generous step limit to avoid infinite running.\n  MAX_STEPS = 500\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      if goal_reached():\n          break\n\n      # Look at the 3\u00d73 neighbourhood for any needed primitive or the workshop.\n      # If something useful is nearby, we ``USE`` it.\n      neighbourhood_kinds = []\n      neighbourhood_kinds.extend(prim_req.keys())\n      if workshop_kind is not None:\n          neighbourhood_kinds.append(workshop_kind)\n\n      # ``next_to`` tells us whether any cell in the 3\u00d73 neighbourhood contains\n      # a given kind.\n      if any(env._current_state.next_to(k) for k in neighbourhood_kinds):\n          actions.append(use_action)\n          env.step(use_action)\n          continue\n\n      # Otherwise, take a random movement action.\n      move = np.random.choice(move_actions)\n      actions.append(move)\n      env.step(move)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
