{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T18:56:59.126783", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of actions that will make the agent obtain a ``stick`` in the\n  given CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation tries to use any planning helper the environment may\n  expose (e.g. a ``plan`` method).  If such a helper is not available we fall\n  back to a very simple deterministic plan that:\n\n  1.  Retrieves the index of the ``stick`` item from the world's cookbook.\n  2.  Queries the recipe for that item to obtain the required primitive(s).\n  3.  For each required primitive we move towards the nearest cell that\n      contains it, perform a ``USE`` action to pick it up, and finally move\n      to the appropriate workshop (again using ``USE``) to craft the stick.\n\n  The fallback plan makes a number of simplifying assumptions that hold for\n  the standard CraftWorld environments used in the tests:\n\n  * The world is fully observable.\n  * The agent can move in the four cardinal directions using actions\n    ``0`` (DOWN), ``1`` (UP), ``2`` (LEFT) and ``3`` (RIGHT).\n  * Action ``4`` corresponds to ``USE`` (collect / craft).\n  * The environment provides ``grid`` (a ``(W, H, K)`` array) and\n    ``init_pos`` (the starting ``(x, y)`` coordinate) via ``env.scenario``.\n  * The world contains at most one instance of each primitive required for a\n    stick, so moving to the first occurrence is sufficient.\n\n  If any of the above assumptions fail the function simply returns an empty\n  action list \u2013 this is safe because the function signature is still\n  honoured and the caller can decide how to handle a no\u2011op plan.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 1. Try to delegate to a built\u2011in planner if the environment offers it\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  try:\n      # Most CraftWorld wrappers expose a ``plan`` method that accepts a goal\n      # name and returns a ready\u2011made action sequence.\n      return env.plan(\"stick\")\n  except Exception:\n      pass  # fall back to the handcrafted planner below\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 2. Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Action constants (these are the defaults used throughout CraftWorld)\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  def manhattan(a, b):\n      \"\"\"Manhattan distance between two (x, y) tuples.\"\"\"\n      return abs(a[0] - b[0]) + abs(a[1] - b[1])\n\n  def move_towards(start, target):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generate a list of movement actions that brings the agent from ``start``\n      to ``target`` using a simple greedy Manhattan strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      x, y = start\n      tx, ty = target\n      actions = []\n      # move in x direction\n      while x < tx:\n          actions.append(DOWN); x += 1\n      while x > tx:\n          actions.append(UP);   x -= 1\n      # move in y direction\n      while y < ty:\n          actions.append(RIGHT); y += 1\n      while y > ty:\n          actions.append(LEFT);  y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 3. Access world objects\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  try:\n      scenario = env.scenario          # CraftScenario instance\n      world = scenario.world           # CraftWorld instance\n      grid = scenario.init_grid.copy() # (W, H, K) occupancy array\n      pos = tuple(scenario.init_pos)   # starting (x, y)\n  except Exception:\n      # If we cannot retrieve the needed attributes we give up.\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 4. Identify indices for stick, its recipe and required primitives\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  try:\n      stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      return []  # stick not defined in this world\n\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  # ``_at`` tells us where the stick must be crafted.\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  # All other keys are ingredient indices.\n  ingredient_indices = [k for k in recipe.keys() if k != \"_at\"]\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 5. Locate each required primitive in the grid\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  actions = []\n  cur_pos = pos\n  for ing_idx in ingredient_indices:\n      # Find the first cell that contains the ingredient.\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, ing_idx] > 0)\n      if locations.size == 0:\n          # Primitive not present \u2013 cannot craft the stick.\n          return []\n      # Choose the closest location (Manhattan distance).\n      distances = [manhattan(cur_pos, tuple(loc)) for loc in locations]\n      target = tuple(locations[np.argmin(distances)])\n      # Move to the primitive.\n      actions.extend(move_towards(cur_pos, target))\n      cur_pos = target\n      # Pick it up.\n      actions.append(USE)\n      # Update the grid to reflect that the primitive has been removed.\n      grid[cur_pos[0], cur_pos[1], ing_idx] = 0\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 6. Move to the workshop (if any) and craft the stick\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      # Find a workshop cell of the required type.\n      ws_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n      if ws_locations.size == 0:\n          return []  # no workshop of the required type\n      distances = [manhattan(cur_pos, tuple(loc)) for loc in ws_locations]\n      ws_target = tuple(ws_locations[np.argmin(distances)])\n      actions.extend(move_towards(cur_pos, ws_target))\n      cur_pos = ws_target\n      # Craft the stick.\n      actions.append(USE)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # 7. Return the compiled action list\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
