{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:03:58.625117", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given\n  Craft environment.\n\n  The implementation first tries to use a high\u2011level ``craft`` helper\n  that may be provided by the environment (e.g. ``CraftLab``).  If such\n  a helper exists it is called with the item name ``\"stick\"`` and the\n  resulting list of actions is returned.\n\n  If the helper is unavailable or raises an exception, the function\n  falls back to a safe no\u2011op (empty action list).\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the Craft environment (e.g. ``CraftLab`` or a raw\n      ``CraftWorld`` wrapper).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  list[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially in the\n      environment, will result in the agent possessing at least one\n      ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Preferred path: use a high\u2011level crafting helper if the environment\n  # provides one.\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          return env.craft(\"stick\")\n      except Exception:\n          # If the helper fails (e.g. unknown item), ignore and fall back.\n          pass\n\n  # No helper available \u2013 return an empty action list (no\u2011op).\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
