{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:20:14.321204", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that, when executed in the given CraftWorld\n  environment, will result in the agent possessing a ``stick`` in its\n  inventory.\n\n  The implementation works generically for any CraftWorld instance:\n    1. Look up the recipe for ``stick``.\n    2. For each required primitive, move to the nearest cell that\n       contains it and issue a ``USE`` action to collect it.\n    3. After all primitives are collected, move to the appropriate\n       workshop (as indicated by the ``_at`` field of the recipe) and\n       issue a ``USE`` action to craft the stick.\n\n  The function does **not** step the environment \u2013 it only returns the\n  sequence of action indices.  The returned actions can be fed to\n  ``env.step(action)`` in order.\n\n  Note\n  ----\n  The exact mapping of action indices is taken from the default\n  CraftWorld definition:\n\n      0 \u2013 DOWN\n      1 \u2013 UP\n      2 \u2013 LEFT\n      3 \u2013 RIGHT\n      4 \u2013 USE\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of ``CraftLab`` (or any wrapper that exposes the same\n      attributes used below: ``world`` and ``_current_state``).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  list[int]\n      Ordered list of actions that will craft a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper: simple Manhattan\u2011grid path planner (no obstacles considered)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def _plan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of movement actions (0\u20113) to go from start to goal.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      y, x = start\n      gy, gx = goal\n      # vertical moves first\n      while y != gy:\n          if gy > y:            # need to go DOWN\n              actions.append(0)\n              y += 1\n          else:                 # need to go UP\n              actions.append(1)\n              y -= 1\n      # then horizontal moves\n      while x != gx:\n          if gx > x:            # need to go RIGHT\n              actions.append(3)\n              x += 1\n          else:                 # need to go LEFT\n              actions.append(2)\n              x -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Begin main routine\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world                     # CraftWorld instance\n  state = env._current_state            # current CraftState\n  grid = state.grid                      # (W, H, n_kinds) array\n  pos = state.pos                        # (y, x) tuple\n\n  # 1\ufe0f\u20e3  Identify the index of the target item (stick)\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index['stick']\n\n  # 2\ufe0f\u20e3  Determine which primitives are required for one stick\n  #     ``primitives_for`` returns a dict {primitive_idx: count}\n  required = world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # Container for the final action sequence\n  plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3\ufe0f\u20e3  Collect each required primitive\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  for prim_idx, needed in required.items():\n      for _ in range(needed):\n          # locate all cells that currently contain the primitive\n          prim_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n          if prim_cells.size == 0:\n              # No primitive left on the map \u2013 abort planning\n              raise RuntimeError(f\"Primitive {prim_idx} not found on the grid.\")\n          # pick the nearest one (Manhattan distance)\n          dists = np.sum(np.abs(prim_cells - np.array(pos)), axis=1)\n          target_cell = prim_cells[dists.argmin()]\n          # move next to the cell (we stop on the cell itself \u2013 the\n          # environment will still allow USE on the same location)\n          plan.extend(_plan_path(pos, tuple(target_cell)))\n          # collect it\n          plan.append(4)                     # USE\n          # Update our simulated position and grid so that the next\n          # iteration works with the new state (lightweight copy).\n          pos = tuple(target_cell)\n          # remove the primitive from the grid (as if it were picked up)\n          grid[pos[0], pos[1], prim_idx] = 0\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4\ufe0f\u20e3  Go to the workshop that can craft a stick and craft it\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The recipe dictionary may contain a special key \"_at\" that tells us\n  # the required workshop kind (as a string, e.g. \"workbench\").\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_name = recipe.get('_at')\n  if workshop_name is not None:\n      wk_idx = world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n      wk_cells = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, wk_idx] > 0)\n      if wk_cells.size == 0:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Workshop '{workshop_name}' not found on the grid.\")\n      dists = np.sum(np.abs(wk_cells - np.array(pos)), axis=1)\n      wk_target = wk_cells[dists.argmin()]\n      plan.extend(_plan_path(pos, tuple(wk_target)))\n      plan.append(4)                         # USE to craft the stick\n\n  return plan", "env_interactions": 4, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:20:35.786574", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a simple action sequence that attempts to craft a ``stick`` in the\n  given Craft environment.\n\n  The implementation follows a very na\u00efve planner:\n    1.  Query the world\u2019s cookbook for the recipe of ``stick``.\n    2.  Determine which primitive items are required and how many of each.\n    3.  Locate the nearest cell containing each required primitive on the\n        current grid and move towards it with Manhattan moves.\n    4.  Use the ``USE`` action (index\u202f4) to pick up the primitive.\n    5.  After all primitives are collected, move to the workshop required by\n        the recipe (if any) and ``USE`` again to craft the stick.\n\n  The planner ignores obstacles and assumes that Manhattan moves are\n  sufficient (which is true for the default CraftWorld maps).  The function\n  returns a list of integer actions that can be fed directly to ``env.step``.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : CraftLab (or compatible) instance\n      The environment to act in.  It must expose the attributes used by the\n      CraftWorld implementation (``world``, ``_current_state`` etc.).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A sequence of actions (0\u202f=\u202fDOWN, 1\u202f=\u202fUP, 2\u202f=\u202fLEFT, 3\u202f=\u202fRIGHT, 4\u202f=\u202fUSE)\n      that, when executed from the initial state, should result in the\n      agent possessing at least one ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Helper: produce Manhattan\u2011style actions from start \u2192 goal.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  def manhattan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of actions moving from start to goal using Manhattan moves.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      x, y = start\n      gx, gy = goal\n      # vertical moves (DOWN / UP)\n      while x < gx:\n          actions.append(0)   # DOWN\n          x += 1\n      while x > gx:\n          actions.append(1)   # UP\n          x -= 1\n      # horizontal moves (RIGHT / LEFT)\n      while y < gy:\n          actions.append(3)   # RIGHT\n          y += 1\n      while y > gy:\n          actions.append(2)   # LEFT\n          y -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Initialise the episode and fetch useful references.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  env.reset()                                 # start a fresh episode\n  state = env._current_state                  # current CraftState\n  world = env.world                           # CraftWorld instance\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Identify the goal index for ``stick`` and fetch its recipe.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  stick_idx = cookbook.index.get(\"stick\")\n  if stick_idx is None:\n      raise ValueError(\"The world does not contain a 'stick' item.\")\n\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  # ``_at`` designates the required workshop; everything else are primitives.\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  primitive_requirements = {\n      int(k): int(v) for k, v in recipe.items() if k != \"_at\"\n  }\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Action list that will be returned.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  plan = []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  # Main planning loop: collect primitives, then craft.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n  while True:\n      # Goal reached?\n      if state.inventory[stick_idx] > 0:\n          break\n\n      # Determine which primitive we still need (if any).\n      missing = {\n          kind: max(0, cnt - state.inventory[kind])\n          for kind, cnt in primitive_requirements.items()\n      }\n      needed_kind = None\n      for kind, cnt in missing.items():\n          if cnt > 0:\n              needed_kind = kind\n              break\n\n      if needed_kind is not None:\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          # Locate the nearest cell that contains the required primitive.\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          locations = np.argwhere(state.grid[:, :, needed_kind] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              raise RuntimeError(\n                  f\"Required primitive (kind {needed_kind}) not present on the map.\"\n              )\n          # Manhattan distance to each candidate location.\n          cur_pos = np.array(state.pos)\n          dists = np.sum(np.abs(locations - cur_pos), axis=1)\n          target_cell = tuple(locations[dists.argmin()])\n\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          # Move to the primitive cell and pick it up.\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          plan.extend(manhattan_path(state.pos, target_cell))\n          plan.append(4)                     # USE to collect\n\n          # Simulate the steps so that subsequent planning uses the updated state.\n          for a in plan[-(len(manhattan_path(state.pos, target_cell)) + 1):]:\n              reward, new_state = env.step(a)\n              state = new_state           # update local reference\n      else:\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          # All primitives collected \u2013 go to the workshop (if required) and craft.\n          # ---------------------------------------------------------- #\n          if workshop_idx is not None:\n              workshop_locs = np.argwhere(state.grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n              if workshop_locs.size == 0:\n                  raise RuntimeError(\"Required workshop not found on the map.\")\n              # choose the first workshop location (any works for this simple planner)\n              target_workshop = tuple(workshop_locs[0])\n              plan.extend(manhattan_path(state.pos, target_workshop))\n              # simulate movement\n              for a in plan[-len(manhattan_path(state.pos, target_workshop)):]:\n                  reward, new_state = env.step(a)\n                  state = new_state\n\n          # Craft the stick.\n          plan.append(4)                     # USE to craft\n          # Final step (craft) \u2013 we don\u2019t need to simulate further; the loop will exit.\n          break\n\n  return plan", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
