{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:26:21.726598", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of actions that will craft a ``stick`` in the given\n  ``CraftWorld`` environment.\n\n  The function tries the following strategies (in order):\n\n  1. If the environment provides a ``plan_to_craft`` method, use it to\n     obtain a plan for the ``stick`` index.\n  2. If the environment provides a ``craft`` method, use it to obtain a\n     plan for the ``stick`` index.\n  3. As a last resort, look up the ``stick`` index in the cookbook and,\n     if the index is found, return an empty plan (the caller can decide\n     how to handle the missing planning capability).\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of a ``CraftWorld`` environment (or a wrapper such as\n      ``CraftLab``) that contains a ``world`` attribute with a ``cookbook``\n      and optionally ``plan_to_craft`` / ``craft`` helper methods.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  list[int]\n      A list of action IDs (e.g. ``0``=DOWN, ``1``=UP, ``2``=LEFT,\n      ``3``=RIGHT, ``4``=USE) that, when executed sequentially, will\n      produce a ``stick`` in the agent's inventory.  An empty list is\n      returned if no planning method is available or the ``stick`` item\n      cannot be located in the recipe index.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Find the integer index that corresponds to the item name \"stick\".\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      # If the index lookup fails we cannot construct a plan.\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Prefer the high\u2011level planning helper if it exists.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan_to_craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.plan_to_craft(stick_idx)\n          # ``plan`` may be any iterable; convert it to a plain list.\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          # If the helper raises, fall back to the next method.\n          pass\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Fall back to the generic ``craft`` method that many wrappers\n  #    expose.  It is expected to return a sequence of actions.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.craft(stick_idx)\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. No automatic planner available \u2013 return an empty plan.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
