{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:29:26.949099", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of low\u2011level action indices that will cause the agent to\n  obtain at least one ``stick`` in the supplied CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation is deliberately generic: it queries the world\u2019s\n  ``Cookbook`` for the index of a stick and then tries to obtain a concrete\n  plan from the environment.  If the environment provides a ``plan_to_craft``\n  helper we use it; otherwise we fall back to a direct ``craft`` call (if\n  available).  When none of these helpers exist an empty plan is returned.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the CraftWorld environment (or a compatible mock).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  list[int]\n      Sequence of action indices that achieve the goal.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Resolve the integer index for the goal item ``stick``.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      # If we cannot resolve the index, we cannot proceed.\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Try to obtain a concrete plan from the environment.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2a. Prefer an explicit planning helper if it exists.\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan_to_craft\"):\n      try:\n          # ``plan_to_craft`` typically expects the goal index and may also\n          # accept a dict of primitive requirements.\n          primitive_requirements = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n          plan = env.plan_to_craft(stick_idx, primitive_requirements)\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          # If the helper fails we fall back to the generic ``craft`` call.\n          pass\n\n  # 2b. Generic ``craft`` method \u2013 some environments expose a simple\n  #     interface that returns a ready\u2011made plan when given the item name\n  #     or index.\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          # First try using the item name.\n          plan = env.craft(\"stick\")\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          try:\n              # If that fails, try using the integer index.\n              plan = env.craft(stick_idx)\n              return list(plan)\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. No planning interface available \u2013 return an empty plan.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:29:28.123927", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  # Try to get stick index\n  try:\n      stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      return []\n  # Use env.craft if exists\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.craft(\"stick\")\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n  # If env has plan_to_craft\n  if hasattr(env, \"plan_to_craft\"):\n      try:\n          plan = env.plan_to_craft(stick_idx)\n          return list(plan)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
