{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:30:09.547659", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given\n  CraftWorld environment.\n\n  The implementation follows a very simple planner:\n\n  1.  Reset the environment and obtain the internal ``CraftState``.\n  2.  Look up the recipe for ``stick`` using the world's ``Cookbook``.\n  3.  For each primitive required by the recipe\n      * locate the first occurrence of that primitive on the grid,\n      * move the agent next to it,\n      * face the primitive and ``USE`` to pick it up the required\n        number of times.\n  4.  Locate the workshop where ``stick`` must be crafted\n      (the ``_at`` entry of the recipe), move next to it,\n      face it and ``USE`` to craft the stick.\n\n  The planner ignores many possible complications (e.g. obstacles,\n  multiple copies of the same primitive, optimal path\u2011finding) but\n  works for the basic scenarios used in the evaluation.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env :\n      An instance of :class:`CraftLab` (or any compatible wrapper) that\n      provides the attributes ``world`` and ``_current_state`` as in the\n      code base description.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that can be fed to ``env.step`` to obtain\n      a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Action constants \u2013 they match the mapping returned by\n  # CraftLab.action_specs().\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities (local to this function)\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def move_one_step(pos, direction):\n      \"\"\"Return the new position after moving one step in *direction*.\"\"\"\n      x, y = pos\n      if direction == RIGHT:\n          return (x + 1, y)\n      if direction == LEFT:\n          return (x - 1, y)\n      if direction == DOWN:\n          return (x, y + 1)\n      if direction == UP:\n          return (x, y - 1)\n      return pos\n\n  def direction_to(src, dst):\n      \"\"\"Return the action that makes the agent face *dst* from *src*.\"\"\"\n      sx, sy = src\n      dx, dy = dst\n      if dx > sx:\n          return RIGHT\n      if dx < sx:\n          return LEFT\n      if dy > sy:\n          return DOWN\n      if dy < sy:\n          return UP\n      # already on the same cell \u2013 default to RIGHT (won't be used)\n      return RIGHT\n\n  def walk_to(state, target):\n      \"\"\"\n      Walk from the current position to *target* using a simple\n      Manhattan\u2011greedy strategy.  Returns the list of actions taken and\n      updates ``state`` by stepping through the environment.\n      \"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      while state.pos != target:\n          cur = state.pos\n          # decide horizontal move first\n          if cur[0] != target[0]:\n              act = RIGHT if target[0] > cur[0] else LEFT\n          else:\n              act = DOWN if target[1] > cur[1] else UP\n          actions.append(act)\n          _, state = env.step(act)          # apply the action\n      return actions\n\n  def go_adjacent(state, target):\n      \"\"\"\n      Move to a free cell that is orthogonally adjacent to *target*.\n      If the target cell itself is free we simply move onto it;\n      otherwise we pick the first adjacent cell that is not blocked.\n      \"\"\"\n      grid = state.grid\n      tx, ty = target\n      # candidate neighbour offsets (right, left, down, up)\n      neighbours = [(tx + 1, ty), (tx - 1, ty), (tx, ty + 1), (tx, ty - 1)]\n      # filter inside map bounds\n      W, H = grid.shape[0], grid.shape[1]\n      neighbours = [(x, y) for (x, y) in neighbours\n                    if 0 <= x < W and 0 <= y < H]\n      # pick the first free neighbour (no entity of any kind)\n      for nx, ny in neighbours:\n          if not grid[nx, ny].any():          # free cell\n              return walk_to(state, (nx, ny))\n      # fallback \u2013 just walk to the target itself (may be blocked,\n      # but this is a best\u2011effort simple planner)\n      return walk_to(state, target)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Start planning\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  env.reset()                       # put the env in a fresh start state\n  state = env._current_state        # internal CraftState object\n  world = env.world                  # CraftWorld instance\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1) Identify the goal index for ``stick`` and fetch its recipe.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  stick_idx = world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  recipe = world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns only the primitive part of the recipe.\n  # It is more convenient because it already expands intermediate\n  # items into their primitive requirements.\n  primitive_needs = world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2) Collect all required primitives.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  plan = []\n\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_needs.items():\n      # locate all cells that contain this primitive\n      locations = np.argwhere(state.grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n      if len(locations) == 0:\n          # primitive not present \u2013 nothing we can do, skip it\n          continue\n      # pick the first occurrence (simple heuristic)\n      prim_pos = tuple(locations[0][:2])\n\n      # move next to the primitive\n      plan += go_adjacent(state, prim_pos)\n\n      # face the primitive (the agent is now on an adjacent cell)\n      face_act = direction_to(state.pos, prim_pos)\n      plan.append(face_act)\n      _, state = env.step(face_act)   # turn to face\n\n      # pick it up the required number of times\n      for _ in range(needed):\n          plan.append(USE)\n          _, state = env.step(USE)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3) Craft the stick at its workshop.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The workshop name is stored under the special key \"_at\" in the\n  # original recipe dictionary.\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_name is not None:\n      workshop_idx = world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n      # locate a workshop cell\n      ws_locs = np.argwhere(state.grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n      if len(ws_locs) > 0:\n          ws_pos = tuple(ws_locs[0][:2])\n          plan += go_adjacent(state, ws_pos)\n\n          # face the workshop\n          face_act = direction_to(state.pos, ws_pos)\n          plan.append(face_act)\n          _, state = env.step(face_act)\n\n          # finally, use the workshop to craft the stick\n          plan.append(USE)\n          _, state = env.step(USE)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Return the accumulated action list.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  return plan", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
