{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:31:14.963814", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a list of actions that will collect the required primitives for a\n  ``stick`` and then craft it at the appropriate workshop.\n\n  The implementation works with the standard CraftLab environment.  It\n  extracts the index of the ``stick`` item from the world cookbook, determines\n  the primitive requirements, finds the closest cells that contain those\n  primitives, moves the agent to them using simple Manhattan moves, picks\n  them up (``USE`` action), then moves to the required workshop and crafts\n  the stick.\n\n  Note: this implementation assumes there are no blocking obstacles between\n  the agent and the target cells (the simple Manhattan planner will work for\n  most generated scenarios).  It does not execute the actions \u2013 it only\n  returns the action list for the caller to step through.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper: simple Manhattan path (no obstacles) from start to goal.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def manhattan_path(start, goal):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of actions (int) that moves from start to goal.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      y, x = start\n      gy, gx = goal\n      # Down (+y) = 0, Up (-y) = 1, Left (-x) = 2, Right (+x) = 3\n      while y < gy:\n          actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n          y += 1\n      while y > gy:\n          actions.append(1)  # UP\n          y -= 1\n      while x < gx:\n          actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          x += 1\n      while x > gx:\n          actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n          x -= 1\n      return actions\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Identify the index of the target item (``stick``) and its recipe.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  stick_name = \"stick\"\n  stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[stick_name]          # integer ID\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns a dict {primitive_idx: count}\n  primitive_requirements = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Gather the current state to locate entities on the grid.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  state = env._current_state                               # current CraftState\n  grid = state.grid                                         # (W, H, n_kinds)\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Collect each required primitive.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n  cur_pos = state.pos                                      # (y, x)\n\n  for prim_idx, needed in primitive_requirements.items():\n      # Find all cells that currently contain this primitive.\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n      if locations.size == 0:\n          # No primitive of this type on the map \u2013 cannot complete task.\n          continue\n      # Simple strategy: repeatedly take the first available location.\n      for _ in range(needed):\n          # Refresh locations in case previous collection removed some.\n          locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n          if locations.size == 0:\n              break\n          target = tuple(locations[0])                     # (y, x)\n\n          # Move to the primitive.\n          actions.extend(manhattan_path(cur_pos, target))\n          cur_pos = target\n\n          # Pick it up.\n          actions.append(4)                               # USE\n          # Update our mental copy of the grid so we don't try to pick the\n          # same item again.\n          grid[target[0], target[1], prim_idx] = 0\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Move to the required workshop and craft the stick.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The workshop index is stored under the special key \"_at\" in the recipe.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_idx = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      # Locate any workshop of this type.\n      workshop_locs = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n      if workshop_locs.size > 0:\n          workshop_pos = tuple(workshop_locs[0])          # (y, x)\n\n          # Move to the workshop.\n          actions.extend(manhattan_path(cur_pos, workshop_pos))\n          cur_pos = workshop_pos\n\n          # Craft the stick.\n          actions.append(4)                               # USE\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
