{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:32:44.524060", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a list of actions that (when executed in the given CraftWorld\n  environment) will result in the agent possessing a ``stick`` in its\n  inventory.\n\n  The implementation works for the standard CraftWorld environment used\n  in the repository:\n\n  * It queries the world\u2019s ``Cookbook`` to obtain the index of the\n    ``stick`` item and the primitive ingredients required to craft it.\n  * It then searches the initial grid for those primitives, plans a\n    Manhattan\u2011style path to each of them (avoiding blocked cells), and\n    inserts a ``USE`` action to pick the item up.\n  * If the ``stick`` itself is a primitive, the function simply collects\n    it.  If it must be crafted, after gathering all required primitives\n    the agent is moved to the appropriate workshop (the workshop type is\n    stored under the ``\"_at\"`` key of the recipe) and a final ``USE``\n    action is issued to perform the crafting.\n\n  The function does **not** modify the environment \u2013 it only inspects the\n  initial state and returns a static list of actions.  The caller is\n  responsible for applying the actions via ``env.step`` (or the equivalent\n  API).\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instantiated CraftWorld environment (e.g. a ``CraftLab`` object).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      Sequence of action indices that will produce a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Helper utilities\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Action ordering used by the environment (as defined in the source):\n  #   0 \u2013 DOWN, 1 \u2013 UP, 2 \u2013 LEFT, 3 \u2013 RIGHT, 4 \u2013 USE\n  ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_UP, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_USE = range(5)\n\n  # Mapping from a movement delta to the corresponding action id.\n  DELTA_TO_ACTION = {\n      ( 1,  0): ACTION_DOWN,\n      (-1,  0): ACTION_UP,\n      ( 0, -1): ACTION_LEFT,\n      ( 0,  1): ACTION_RIGHT,\n  }\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 1. Reset the environment to obtain the initial state.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  try:\n      env.reset()\n  except Exception:            # pragma: no cover \u2013 defensive fallback\n      # If the environment does not expose a reset method we simply give up.\n      return []\n\n  # The internal state is stored in a private attribute.\n  try:\n      state = env._current_state          # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n  except AttributeError:                 # pragma: no cover\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 2. Extract useful world information.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  world = env.world                         # the CraftWorld object\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  grid = state.grid                         # (W, H, n_kinds) uint8 array\n  pos = tuple(state.pos)                    # (row, col)\n\n  # Resolve the index of the item named \"stick\".\n  try:\n      stick_idx = cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:                       # pragma: no cover\n      # No stick defined \u2013 nothing we can do.\n      return []\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 3. Determine the recipe for the stick.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # ``primitives_for`` returns a dict {primitive_idx: count}.\n  # If the dict is empty, the stick is a primitive that can be collected\n  # directly.\n  primitive_requirements = cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  # ``_at`` key (if present) tells us where the crafting must happen.\n  # The recipe is stored in ``cookbook.recipes``.\n  recipe = cookbook.recipes.get(stick_idx, {})\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\", None)\n  if workshop_name is not None:\n      workshop_idx = cookbook.index.get(workshop_name, None)\n  else:\n      workshop_idx = None\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 4. Utility: locate the *nearest* cell that contains a given kind.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  def find_nearest(kind_idx, start):\n      \"\"\"Return a path (list of actions) from ``start`` to the closest cell\n      that contains an entity of type ``kind_idx``.  Returns ``None`` if\n      no such cell exists.\"\"\"\n      # Identify all cells that contain the desired kind.\n      locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, kind_idx] > 0)\n      if locations.size == 0:\n          return None\n\n      # Simple Manhattan\u2011distance heuristic \u2013 pick the closest cell.\n      dists = np.abs(locations[:, 0] - start[0]) + np.abs(locations[:, 1] - start[1])\n      target = tuple(locations[dists.argmin()])\n\n      # BFS on the 2\u2011D grid (ignoring the third dimension).  A cell is\n      # traversable if *no* kind is present there (i.e. the sum across\n      # kinds is zero) or if it is the target cell itself.\n      W, H = grid.shape[:2]\n      blocked = np.any(grid > 0, axis=2)          # True where something exists\n      blocked[target] = False                    # allow stepping onto target\n\n      queue = collections.deque()\n      queue.append((start, []))\n      visited = np.full((W, H), False, dtype=bool)\n      visited[start] = True\n\n      while queue:\n          (r, c), path = queue.popleft()\n          if (r, c) == target:\n              return path\n\n          for dr, dc in [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n              nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n              if 0 <= nr < W and 0 <= nc < H and not visited[nr, nc] and not blocked[nr, nc]:\n                  visited[nr, nc] = True\n                  action = DELTA_TO_ACTION[(dr, dc)]\n                  queue.append(((nr, nc), path + [action]))\n      return None  # No reachable path\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 5. Gather all required primitives.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  actions = []\n  cur_pos = pos\n\n  # If the stick itself is a primitive, treat it as the only required item.\n  if not primitive_requirements:\n      # Need to pick up the stick directly.\n      primitive_requirements = {stick_idx: 1}\n\n  for prim_idx, count in primitive_requirements.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          path = find_nearest(prim_idx, cur_pos)\n          if path is None:                     # pragma: no cover \u2013 safety\n              return []                        # cannot reach required primitive\n          actions.extend(path)\n          actions.append(ACTION_USE)           # pick it up\n          # Update the simulated position.\n          for a in path:\n              dr, dc = {\n                  ACTION_DOWN: (1, 0),\n                  ACTION_UP:   (-1, 0),\n                  ACTION_LEFT: (0, -1),\n                  ACTION_RIGHT:(0, 1),\n              }[a]\n              cur_pos = (cur_pos[0] + dr, cur_pos[1] + dc)\n\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # 6. If crafting is required, move to the appropriate workshop and craft.\n  # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if workshop_idx is not None:\n      path = find_nearest(workshop_idx, cur_pos)\n      if path is None:                         # pragma: no cover\n          return []                            # cannot reach workshop\n      actions.extend(path)\n      actions.append(ACTION_USE)               # perform the crafting\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
