{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:35:28.643468", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given\n  Craft environment.\n\n  The implementation attempts to use a high\u2011level ``craft`` helper if the\n  environment provides one (as is typical for the reference implementation\n  in this repository).  This helper is expected to accept the name of the\n  desired item and return a list of integer actions that will collect the\n  necessary primitives and perform the crafting operation at the appropriate\n  workshop.\n\n  If the helper is not available, the function falls back to returning an\n  empty list (a no\u2011op).  Callers can decide how to handle the empty plan.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of the Craft environment (e.g. ``CraftLab`` or a raw\n      ``CraftWorld`` wrapper).\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list of action indices that, when executed sequentially in the\n      environment, will result in the agent possessing at least one\n      ``stick``.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Preferred path: use the high\u2011level crafting helper if it exists.\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          # ``env.craft`` should accept the name of the desired item and\n          # return a ready\u2011to\u2011execute action list.\n          return env.craft(\"stick\")\n      except Exception:\n          # If the helper raises (e.g. unknown item), fall back to safe default.\n          pass\n\n  # If no helper is available, we cannot construct a plan without deeper\n  # knowledge of the grid layout.  Returning an empty list is a safe no\u2011op.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:35:29.790403", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given Craft environment.\n  \"\"\"\n  # try high-level helper\n  if hasattr(env, \"craft\"):\n      try:\n          return env.craft(\"stick\")\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n  # fallback: try to access world.cookbook and plan naive\n  # simple fallback: return empty list\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:35:48.704678", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:35:49.870495", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Returns a minimal action sequence that will make a stick in the given\n  CraftWorld environment.  In the simplest case the environment is already\n  set up so that a single ``USE`` action (action index 4) will craft the\n  stick.  This implementation therefore returns a list containing only that\n  action.\n\n  Args:\n      env: An instance of the CraftWorld / CraftLab environment.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: A list of action indices that can be executed by the\n      environment to obtain a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Action index for the ``USE`` operation as defined by CraftLab.action_specs()\n  USE = 4\n  return [USE]", "env_interactions": 1, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
