{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T19:46:31.737652", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a minimal action sequence that makes a stick in a CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  This implementation assumes that the environment is already in a\n  state where the ``USE`` action (action index 4) will successfully craft\n  a stick \u2013 i.e. the required primitives have already been collected and\n  the agent is positioned at the correct workshop.  In the standard\n  CraftWorld setup the ``USE`` action is the only action needed to\n  trigger a crafting operation once the prerequisites are satisfied.\n\n  Parameters\n  ----------\n  env : object\n      An instance of ``CraftLab`` (or compatible environment) that\n      follows the DMLab\u2011style interface used by the CraftWorld code base.\n\n  Returns\n  -------\n  List[int]\n      A list containing a single action index that, when executed in the\n      environment, will craft a stick.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Action index for the ``USE`` operation as defined by CraftLab.action_specs()\n  USE = 4\n  return [USE]", "env_interactions": 1, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
