{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T20:22:07.877978", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a sequence of actions that would make a stick in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.  In this simplified implementation we return an empty list,\n  which represents a no\u2011op.  The function signature matches the expected\n  interface and can be extended later with a proper planning algorithm.\n\n  Args:\n      env: An instance of the CraftWorld / CraftLab environment.\n\n  Returns:\n      List[int]: An (initially empty) list of action indices.\n  \"\"\"\n  # No actions are defined in this minimal placeholder implementation.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T20:22:09.031250", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Return a sequence of actions that makes a ``stick`` in the given CraftWorld\n  environment.\n\n  The :class:`CraftWorld` environment exposes a ``craft`` method that,\n  given the name of an item, returns a list of action indices which, when\n  executed, will collect the necessary primitives, move to the appropriate\n  workshop and perform the crafting operation.\n\n  If the environment does not provide such a method (or an error occurs)\n  the function falls back to returning an empty list \u2013 a no\u2011op plan.\n  \"\"\"\n  try:\n      # The environment's ``craft`` helper builds a valid action sequence.\n      return env.craft('stick')\n  except Exception:\n      # In case the helper is unavailable, return an empty (no\u2011op) plan.\n      return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
