{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T20:31:02.224180", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Plan and return a sequence of actions to craft a stick in the given CraftWorld environment.\n  The function extracts the recipe for a stick, gathers required primitives,\n  moves the agent to collect them, and finally performs the crafting action.\n  \"\"\"\n  # Identify the index for the 'stick' item\n  stick_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # Retrieve primitive requirements for a stick\n  required = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(stick_idx)\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # Helper to move towards a target cell (simple Manhattan approach)\n  def move_to(target):\n      while env._current_state.pos[0] < target[0]:\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 1)  # DOWN\n          env.step(actions[-1])\n      while env._current_state.pos[0] > target[0]:\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 2)  # UP\n          env.step(actions[-1])\n      while env._current_state.pos[1] < target[1]:\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 3)  # RIGHT\n          env.step(actions[-1])\n      while env._current_state.pos[1] > target[1]:\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 4)  # LEFT\n          env.step(actions[-1])\n\n  # Collect each required primitive\n  for prim_idx, count in required.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          # Find nearest cell containing the primitive\n          positions = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, prim_idx] > 0)\n          if len(positions) == 0:\n              continue\n          # Choose the first found position (could be optimized)\n          target_pos = tuple(positions[0])\n          move_to(target_pos)\n          # Face the primitive (assume direction doesn't matter for USE)\n          actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 5)  # USE to pick up\n          env.step(actions[-1])\n\n  # Move to a workshop that can craft sticks (assume any workshop works)\n  workshop_idx = env.world.workshop_indices[0]\n  workshop_positions = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, workshop_idx] > 0)\n  if len(workshop_positions) > 0:\n      move_to(tuple(workshop_positions[0]))\n\n  # Craft the stick\n  actions.append(env.world.n_actions - 5)  # USE to craft\n  env.step(actions[-1])\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
