{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T20:33:11.149478", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Generate a sequence of actions that will result in the agent possessing a\n  ``stick`` in its inventory.\n\n  The implementation works for any ``CraftWorld`` / ``CraftLab`` environment\n  that follows the API described in the specification.  It extracts the\n  recipe for ``stick`` from the world's ``Cookbook``, navigates to each required\n  primitive, picks it up, then moves to the appropriate workshop and crafts\n  the stick.\n\n  The returned list contains integer action IDs as defined by the environment\n  (0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT, 4=USE).\n  \"\"\"\n  # get indices\n  idx_stick = env.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  # find required primitives\n  needed = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(idx_stick)  # dict {prim_idx: count}\n  actions = []\n\n  # helper to find nearest cell containing a given kind\n  def locate(kind_idx):\n      grid = env._current_state.grid if hasattr(env, \"_current_state\") else env.scenario.init_grid\n      # grid shape (W,H,K)\n      w, h, _ = grid.shape\n      pos = env._current_state.pos if hasattr(env, \"_current_state\") else env.scenario.init_pos\n      # BFS to nearest cell with kind_idx\n      from collections import deque\n      visited = set()\n      q = deque([(pos, [])])\n      while q:\n          (x, y), path = q.popleft()\n          if (x, y) in visited:\n              continue\n          visited.add((x, y))\n          if grid[x, y, kind_idx] > 0:\n              return path\n          # explore neighbours\n          for a, (dx, dy) in enumerate([(0,1),(0,-1),(-1,0),(1,0)]):\n              nx, ny = x+dx, y+dy\n              if 0 <= nx < w and 0 <= ny < h and (nx, ny) not in visited:\n                  q.append(((nx, ny), path+[a]))\n      return None\n\n  # collect each primitive the required number of times\n  for prim_idx, count in needed.items():\n      for _ in range(count):\n          path = locate(prim_idx)\n          if path is None:\n              continue\n          actions.extend(path)\n          actions.append(4)   # USE to pick up\n\n  # move to workshop for stick if any (_at key)\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(idx_stick, {})\n  workshop_name = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_name:\n      wk_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name]\n      path = locate(wk_idx)\n      if path:\n          actions.extend(path)\n  # finally craft\n  actions.append(4)  # USE at workshop\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 5, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
