{"timestamp": "2025-10-15T20:38:21.694428", "function_name": "make_stick", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Simple planner that moves the agent to the nearest *stick* primitive (if it\n  exists) and uses the ``USE`` action to pick it up.  The function works\n  with both ``CraftLab`` and raw ``CraftWorld`` environments that expose the\n  internal ``CraftState`` via ``env._current_state`` after a reset.\n\n  The returned list of integer actions follows the action ordering used by\n  ``CraftLab.action_specs()``:\n\n      0 \u2192 DOWN\n      1 \u2192 UP\n      2 \u2192 LEFT\n      3 \u2192 RIGHT\n      4 \u2192 USE\n\n  If a stick cannot be found (e.g. it is not a primitive or the recipe is\n  missing) the function returns an empty action list.\n  \"\"\"\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 1. Reset the environment and obtain the current state object.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  _ = env.reset()\n  # ``CraftLab`` stores the state in a private attribute; ``CraftWorld`` can\n  # be handled similarly because after a reset it also creates a\n  # ``CraftState`` instance.\n  state = getattr(env, \"_current_state\", None)\n  if state is None:\n      # Fallback for environments that directly expose the state.\n      state = getattr(env, \"state\", None)\n  if state is None:\n      return []          # cannot proceed without a state object\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 2. Resolve the integer index for the item named \"stick\".\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  try:\n      stick_idx = state.world.cookbook.index[\"stick\"]\n  except Exception:\n      return []          # no such item in the index\n\n  # If the stick is a primitive (i.e. can be collected directly) we can\n  # attempt to locate it on the map.\n  if stick_idx not in state.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      # Non\u2011primitive items would require crafting logic which is beyond\n      # the scope of this simple planner.\n      return []\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 3. Locate the nearest cell that contains a stick primitive.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  grid = state.grid[:, :, stick_idx]          # 2\u2011D occupancy of sticks\n  stick_positions = list(zip(*np.where(grid > 0)))\n  if not stick_positions:\n      return []          # no sticks present on the map\n\n  start = state.pos\n  # Simple BFS over the 2\u2011D grid (ignoring the third dimension).  A cell is\n  # traversable if *all* kinds have a zero count there (i.e. it is empty).\n  height, width = grid.shape\n  def is_free(x, y):\n      # Any non\u2011zero entry in the full grid blocks movement.\n      return not state.grid[x, y, :].any()\n\n  # BFS queue stores (x, y, path) where path is a list of (dx, dy) moves.\n  from collections import deque\n  q = deque()\n  visited = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=bool)\n  q.append((start[0], start[1], []))\n  visited[start[0], start[1]] = True\n\n  target_path = None\n  while q:\n      x, y, path = q.popleft()\n      if (x, y) in stick_positions:\n          target_path = path\n          break\n      for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:   # UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT\n          nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n          if 0 <= nx < height and 0 <= ny < width and not visited[nx, ny]:\n              if is_free(nx, ny) or (nx, ny) in stick_positions:\n                  visited[nx, ny] = True\n                  q.append((nx, ny, path + [(dx, dy)]))\n\n  if target_path is None:\n      return []          # no reachable stick found\n\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # 4. Convert the path of (dx, dy) moves into the integer action IDs.\n  # --------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n  # Action mapping (consistent with CraftLab.action_specs):\n  #   DOWN \u2192 0  (dx = +1, dy = 0)\n  #   UP   \u2192 1  (dx = -1, dy = 0)\n  #   LEFT \u2192 2  (dx = 0, dy = -1)\n  #   RIGHT\u2192 3  (dx = 0, dy = +1)\n  move_to_action = {\n      ( 1,  0): 0,   # DOWN\n      (-1,  0): 1,   # UP\n      ( 0, -1): 2,   # LEFT\n      ( 0,  1): 3,   # RIGHT\n  }\n\n  actions = [move_to_action[(dx, dy)] for dx, dy in target_path]\n\n  # After arriving on the stick cell we need to pick it up.\n  actions.append(4)   # USE action\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
